1
00:00:02,190 --> 00:00:07,204
The Life Of Muhammad ﷺ, Madinan Period Volume 2

2
00:00:07,755 --> 00:00:09,706
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:10,218 --> 00:00:11,728
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝

4
00:00:12,199 --> 00:00:13,633
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

5
00:00:14,368 --> 00:00:19,849
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

6
00:00:20,650 --> 00:00:23,539
Rasool Allah ﷺ opened Makkah,

7
00:00:24,063 --> 00:00:32,867
the strongest resistance, that Rasool Allah ﷺ was receiving was ended, that is Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

8
00:00:33,555 --> 00:00:39,853
But now, there was another tribe which held prominence in the land of Hijaz(حجاز).

9
00:00:40,764 --> 00:00:46,540
In fact, when the Kuffar(كفار) were questioning the Prophethood of Muhammadﷺ

10
00:00:47,230 --> 00:00:51,623
they came up with suggestions of who should become the Prophet.

11
00:00:52,262 --> 00:00:59,973
They said: Why wasn't this Qur'an revealed on one man from the two villages?

12
00:01:00,516 --> 00:01:06,101
  وَقَالُوا لَوْلَا نُزِّلَ هَٰذَا الْقُرْآنُ عَلَىٰ رَجُلٍ مِنَ الْقَرْيَتَيْنِ عَظِيمٍ۝

13
00:01:06,629 --> 00:01:12,373
And what they meant by the two villages or towns is Makkah and At-Taef(ألطائف)

14
00:01:12,705 --> 00:01:15,371
and At-Taef(ألطائف), the tribe of Thaqeef(ثقيف) live there.

15
00:01:16,110 --> 00:01:18,965
And the tribe of the Thaqeef(ثقيف) are the branch of Hawazin(هوازن).

16
00:01:19,473 --> 00:01:26,282
Hawazin(هوازن) is a big mother tribe and then there's many sub tribes that descend from Hawazin(هوازن).

17
00:01:27,271 --> 00:01:33,921
They used to see themselves as prominent and important, just like Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

18
00:01:34,878 --> 00:01:37,841
And there was some competition between the two tribes,

19
00:01:38,103 --> 00:01:42,479
because of the Jahilliyah(جاهلية) and the tribalism of Jahilliyah(جاهلية).

20
00:01:43,433 --> 00:01:48,889
They didn't want a man from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) to take over their land and rule over them.

21
00:01:49,791 --> 00:01:51,633
And this is what they saw coming.

22
00:01:53,019 --> 00:01:57,995
They felt that since Rasool Allah ﷺ has now opened Makkah, we're going to be next

23
00:01:58,035 --> 00:02:00,397
because At-Taef(ألطائف) was very close.

24
00:02:00,987 --> 00:02:07,577
Plus they have a sour history, when it comes to the treatment of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

25
00:02:07,704 --> 00:02:13,259
Remember what the people of At-Taef(ألطائف) did to Muhammadﷺ, when he went to them calling,

26
00:02:13,299 --> 00:02:14,269
لا إله الا الله,

27
00:02:14,339 --> 00:02:23,262
how they treated him, very bad, very evil, where's the generosity, where's the treatment of your guests?

28
00:02:23,293 --> 00:02:25,908
Even if you disagree with your guest.

29
00:02:26,052 --> 00:02:33,622
The way they treated the Rasool Allah ﷺ was bad, even by the standards of the time.

30
00:02:34,997 --> 00:02:37,956
And that was a very difficult day on Rasool Allah ﷺ.

31
00:02:38,224 --> 00:02:46,861
So, Malik Ibn Auf An-Nasri(مالك إبن عوف أنصري), he tried to mobilize the various tribes of Hawazin(هوازن),

32
00:02:46,934 --> 00:02:49,131
some of them accepted his call and some didn't.

33
00:02:49,604 --> 00:02:54,434
He was able to pull together a very strong coalition, very strong, powerful army.

34
00:02:55,001 --> 00:02:56,310
And these were good fighters.

35
00:02:56,721 --> 00:03:02,748
Rasool Allah ﷺ heard the news and he marched out of Makkah, in an army of 12,000.

36
00:03:03,194 --> 00:03:06,471
He had 10,000 with him, when he entered into Makkah.

37
00:03:06,843 --> 00:03:10,539
And now he was accompanied by 2000 from a At-Tulaqaa(ألطلقآء),

38
00:03:10,626 --> 00:03:12,483
At-Tulaqaa(ألطلقآء) are the released ones.

39
00:03:12,780 --> 00:03:18,413
We talked about them, the ones whom Rasool Allah ﷺ released on the day of the conquest of Makkah.

40
00:03:18,493 --> 00:03:20,572
 These are the people of Makkah, who became Muslim.

41
00:03:21,445 --> 00:03:26,783
The army was large, and Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابو بكر الصديق) and probably some others said;

42
00:03:27,030 --> 00:03:28,916
لَنْ نُغْلَبْ اَلْيَوْمْ مِنْ قِلَّةْ

43
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:32,501
We're not going to be defeated today due to lack of numbers.

44
00:03:33,307 --> 00:03:40,714
Our numbers are great and you will see the consequences of this belief.

45
00:03:41,593 --> 00:03:46,110
When Malik(مالك) brought together his army and they set out,

46
00:03:46,693 --> 00:03:49,384
they were accompanied by a wise old man,

47
00:03:49,844 --> 00:03:57,332
a man who was famous, a man who was a well known knight, fighter in his youth,

48
00:03:57,766 --> 00:04:01,568
and a very prominent poet among the Arabs,

49
00:04:01,861 --> 00:04:04,469
and his name is Duraid Ibn Simmah(دريد بن الصمة).

50
00:04:05,260 --> 00:04:11,036
Duraid(دريد) was blind at that time, and very frail, old in age

51
00:04:11,774 --> 00:04:17,876
and there was this conversation that occurred between Duraid(دريد) and Malik(مالك).

52
00:04:19,390 --> 00:04:23,340
قَالَ: دُرَيْدْ بِاَيِّ وَادٍ اَنْتُمْ ؟ فَقَالُوا: بِاُوْطَاسْ

53
00:04:23,657 --> 00:04:25,048
Duraid(دريد) said: Where are we?

54
00:04:25,088 --> 00:04:26,571
They said: We are in Autaas(أوطاس).

55
00:04:26,822 --> 00:04:32,766
قَالَ: نِعْمَ مَجَالْ اَلْخَيْلَ لَا حَزَنٌ ضَرْسٌ، وَلَا سَهْلٌ دَهْسٌ

56
00:04:33,529 --> 00:04:35,977
He said: A fine place for cavalry.

57
00:04:36,286 --> 00:04:39,255
It's neither hilly with rocks, nor is it soft ground.

58
00:04:39,509 --> 00:04:41,207
So he liked the location.

59
00:04:41,835 --> 00:04:42,593
And then he said;

60
00:04:43,105 --> 00:04:48,490
مَا لِيْ اَسْمَعُ رُغَاءَ الْبَعِيْرَ، وَنَهَاقَ الْحَمِيْرْ ، وَيُعَارَ الشَّاءْ، وَبُكَاءَ الصَّغِيْرَ ؟

61
00:04:48,768 --> 00:04:51,785
Why is it? That I hear the granting of camels,

62
00:04:51,992 --> 00:04:56,790
the braying of donkeys, the bleating of sheep, and the crying of babies.

63
00:04:57,271 --> 00:04:58,959
Malik Bin Auf(مالك بن عوف), what he did.?

64
00:04:59,696 --> 00:05:06,797
He brought along with the army, their women, their children, their cattle, everything.

65
00:05:07,635 --> 00:05:13,890
And his reasoning for that is, he thought that this would prevent them from running away.

66
00:05:14,535 --> 00:05:18,019
Because if they run away, they will realize that they will lose everything

67
00:05:18,043 --> 00:05:19,740
because the Muslims will take it over.

68
00:05:21,238 --> 00:05:23,275
قَالُوْ: سَاقَةْ مَالِكْ مَعَ النَّاسَ ذَالِكْ

69
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:25,063
They told him, This is what Malik(مالك) did?

70
00:05:25,087 --> 00:05:28,055
He brought with the people all of their wealth.

71
00:05:28,624 --> 00:05:31,825
فَقَالَ: يَا مَالِك اِنَّ هَذَا يَوْمُ لَّهُمَا بَعْدَه

72
00:05:32,290 --> 00:05:34,744
And you can see through this discussion,

73
00:05:34,928 --> 00:05:37,857
the difference in perception between the young and the old,

74
00:05:37,897 --> 00:05:40,912
and the man who has experience and the young who doesn't,

75
00:05:41,444 --> 00:05:45,505
and the wisdom of an old warrior, Duraid Ibn Simmah(دريد بن الصمة).

76
00:05:46,073 --> 00:05:52,012
And you can see in it, Malik Bin Auf(مالك بن عوف) aspiring young man,

77
00:05:52,036 --> 00:05:56,308
who wants to make a victory for himself and a name for himself

78
00:05:56,332 --> 00:06:00,020
and he's taking large and unnecessary risk.

79
00:06:01,211 --> 00:06:05,150
 فَقَالَ: يَا مَالِك اِنَّ هَذَا يَوْمُ لَّهُمَا بَعْدَه

80
00:06:05,175 --> 00:06:11,531
O Malik(مالك)! This day has great consequences for the future, this is not a normal day.

81
00:06:11,555 --> 00:06:13,283
اِنَّ هَذَا يَوْمُ لَّهُمَا بَعْدَه

82
00:06:14,023 --> 00:06:16,231
This day will determine our future.

83
00:06:16,422 --> 00:06:18,246
مَا حَمَلَكَ عَلَى مَا صَنَعْت

84
00:06:18,271 --> 00:06:21,117
Why did you do, what you have done?

85
00:06:22,027 --> 00:06:26,755
قَالَ: سُقْتُهُمْ مَعَ النَّاْسِ لِيُقَاتِلَ كُلَّ اِنْسَاٍن عنْ حَرِيْمِهِ وَمَالِه

86
00:06:27,059 --> 00:06:32,636
I brought them with the army, so that everyone would fight for his family and his wealth.

87
00:06:33,346 --> 00:06:37,239
قَالَ دُرَيْد:رَاعِيْ ضَاْنٍ وَالله، هَلْ يَرُدُّ الْمُنْهَزِمْ شَىْء؟

88
00:06:37,813 --> 00:06:42,334
اِنَّهَا اِنْ كَانَتْ لَكْ لَمْ يَنْفَعَكَ اِلَّا رَجُلٌ بِسَيْفِهِ وَرُمْحِهِ

89
00:06:43,414 --> 00:06:46,608
 وَاِنْ كَانَتْ عَلَيْكَ فُضِحْتَ فِيْ اَهْلِكَ وَمَالِكْ

90
00:06:46,632 --> 00:06:51,571
He said: You sheep grazer, would anything ever turned around someone in retreat.

91
00:06:51,989 --> 00:06:58,283
If the battle is to go well, it will be only men with swords and lances, who do you good?

92
00:06:58,984 --> 00:07:00,455
If the battle goes badly,

93
00:07:00,673 --> 00:07:04,922
you'll be disgraced with regards to your family and possessions anyway.

94
00:07:05,121 --> 00:07:08,839
He said: Nothing will turn back a person who's in retreat.

95
00:07:08,871 --> 00:07:11,995
When a person is afraid, they're not going to think about anything, they are gonna flee away.

96
00:07:12,382 --> 00:07:13,300
And then he asked him;

97
00:07:13,636 --> 00:07:15,887
وَقَالَ: مَا فَعَلَتْ كَعْبٌ وَكُلَابْ؟

98
00:07:16,633 --> 00:07:18,431
What did Ka'ab(كعب) and Kalaab(كلاب) do?

99
00:07:18,471 --> 00:07:20,582
These are two tribes of Hawazin(هوازن)

100
00:07:20,995 --> 00:07:22,561
قَالُوْ: لَمْ يَشْهَدُهَا اَحَدًا مِنْهُمْ

101
00:07:23,549 --> 00:07:25,939
None of them, have came.

102
00:07:26,576 --> 00:07:30,235
قَالَ: غَابَ الْحِدّ وَالْجَدْ، لَوْ كَانَ يَوْمَ عَلَاءٍ وَرِفْعَةْ

103
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:35,103
لَمْ تَغِبْ عَنْه’ كَعْبٌ وَكُلَابْ، وَلَوْ دَدْتُ اَنَّكُمْ فَعَلْتُمْ مَا فَعَلَ

104
00:07:35,372 --> 00:07:36,964
No one of them is present, they said,

105
00:07:37,020 --> 00:07:40,670
and then he said: So then skill and courage are absent.

106
00:07:41,192 --> 00:07:46,068
If it were to be a day of fine noble deeds Ka'ab(كعب) and Kalaab(كلاب) would not miss it.

107
00:07:46,375 --> 00:07:48,587
I wish you had done the same as them.

108
00:07:50,450 --> 00:07:50,964
And then he said;

109
00:07:50,988 --> 00:07:51,981
فَمَنْ شَهِدَهَا مَعَكُمْ؟

110
00:07:52,005 --> 00:07:52,799
So, who's with you.

111
00:07:53,216 --> 00:07:55,285
قَالُوْ: عَمْرُوْ بِن عامر، وَعَوفْ بن عامر

112
00:07:56,084 --> 00:07:59,890
They said: Amr Bin Aamir(عمرو بن عامر) and Auf Bin Aamir(عوف بن عامر), these are two clans.

113
00:08:00,215 --> 00:08:03,143
قَالَ:ذَالِكَ الْجَذْعَانْ مِنْ عَامِر لَا يَنْفَعَانْ وَلَا يَضُرَّانْ

114
00:08:03,561 --> 00:08:07,126
Well those two branches of Aamir(عامر) will do neither good nor harm.

115
00:08:07,685 --> 00:08:14,070
ثُمَّ قَالَ: يَا مَالِكْ، اِنَّكَ لَمْ تَصْنَعْ بِتَقْدِيْمِ الْبَيْضَةْ هَوَازِنْ اِلَى نَحُوْرُ الْخَيْلِ شَيْئَا،

116
00:08:14,692 --> 00:08:16,005
He then said to Malik(مالك):

117
00:08:16,295 --> 00:08:22,746
You have done nothing by sending ahead the main force of Hawazin(هوازن) to face up, to the cavalry.

118
00:08:23,820 --> 00:08:29,044
So, he saw it, as suicide and then he gave his recommendation.

119
00:08:29,532 --> 00:08:33,280
ثُمَّ قَالَ يَا مالك: اِرْفَعْ مَن مَّعَكَ اِلَى عَلْيَا بِلَادِهِمْ

120
00:08:33,831 --> 00:08:37,260
ثُمَّ الْقِ الصُّبِي عَلَى الْخَيْل اَوْ الصِبَّا عَلَى الْخَيْلْ

121
00:08:37,840 --> 00:08:40,889
فَاِنْ كَانَتْ لَكَ لَحِقَ بِكَ مِنْ وَّرَائَكْ

122
00:08:41,229 --> 00:08:44,392
وَاِنْ كَانَتْ عَلَيْكْ كُنْتَ قَدْ اَحْرَزْتَ اَهْلَكَ وَمَالَكْ

123
00:08:44,992 --> 00:08:52,901
He said: O Malik(مالك) take away the families and the cattle up to the high lands of Hawazin(هوازن),

124
00:08:53,413 --> 00:08:59,366
the fortified lands, in the mountains take them to the mountain parts of our land.

125
00:09:00,096 --> 00:09:03,729
And then meet the apostates, As-Suba'a(أصباء).

126
00:09:03,951 --> 00:09:05,851
This is the name they used to call the Muslims.

127
00:09:06,162 --> 00:09:09,287
Meet the apostates on horseback.

128
00:09:10,035 --> 00:09:19,928
If it is for you, then the rest would come, if it is against you, then you have at least protected your family and your wealth.

129
00:09:20,760 --> 00:09:22,889
Malik(مالك) responded by saying;

130
00:09:22,913 --> 00:09:24,432
وَالله لَا اَفْعَل ذلك

131
00:09:24,499 --> 00:09:26,382
In the name of Allah, I'm not going to do that.

132
00:09:26,668 --> 00:09:28,728
اِنَّكَ قَدْ كَبُرْتَ وَكَبُرَ عِلْمُكْ

133
00:09:29,037 --> 00:09:31,940
You are an old man and your knowledge is becoming old.

134
00:09:32,263 --> 00:09:37,686
وَالله لَتُطِيْعَنَّنِيْ يَا مَعْشَرَ هَوَازِنْ اَوْ لَا تَكِئَنَّ عَلَى هَذَا السَّيْفَ حَتَّى يَخْرُجُ مِنْ ظَهْرِيْ

135
00:09:37,877 --> 00:09:42,797
O Hawazin(هوازن), you will either follow me or I'm going to jump on top of this sword.

136
00:09:42,821 --> 00:09:46,892
He put this sword on the ground, with the base down and the tip of it on the top.

137
00:09:47,061 --> 00:09:51,584
And he said: I'm going to jump on this sword and kill myself, until, it comes out from my back.

138
00:09:51,917 --> 00:09:54,098
وَكَرِه اَنْ يَكُوْنُ لِدُرَيْد فِيْهَا ذِكْرًا

139
00:09:54,122 --> 00:09:56,571
And he didn't want Duraid(دريد) to have any involvement.

140
00:09:57,021 --> 00:09:59,759
فَقَالَ دُرَيْد: هَذَا يَوْم لَمْ اَشْهَدْهُ وَلَمْ يُفَتْنِيْ

141
00:10:00,303 --> 00:10:02,971
This is a the day that I'm not counted as part of it.

142
00:10:03,717 --> 00:10:07,912
Duraid(دريد) didn't want, to have anything to do with the consequences of this battle

143
00:10:07,956 --> 00:10:11,453
 and he made it clear, he gave them, his opinion they refused to take it.

144
00:10:11,629 --> 00:10:15,649
So, he wants to make it clear that I'm not responsible for the consequences.

145
00:10:16,830 --> 00:10:24,498
ثُمَّ قَالَ مَالك: اَيُّهَا النَّاسْ: اِذَا رَاَيْتُمُوْهُمُ الْقَوْمَ فَاكْسِرُوْا جَفُوْنَ سُيُوْفِكُمْ،وَ شُدُّوْعَلَيْهِمْ شَدَّةَ رَجُلٍ وَّاحِدْ

146
00:10:24,522 --> 00:10:31,961
O men, when you see the enemy, break the sheaths of your swords and attack them as one man,

147
00:10:32,276 --> 00:10:34,090
meaning all of you attacking the same time.

148
00:10:35,827 --> 00:10:41,882
Rasool Allah ﷺ has sent Abdullah Bin Abi Hazrad(عبد الله بن أبي حدرد) to gather intelligence for him.

149
00:10:42,933 --> 00:10:47,057
So, Abdullah Bin Abi Hazrad(عبد الله بن أبي حدرد) came back to Rasool Allah ﷺ and told him, what he saw?

150
00:10:47,081 --> 00:10:48,683
He infiltrated the army and

151
00:10:49,171 --> 00:10:55,390
was able to see the numbers, and to see the families, and to see the cattle of Hawazin(هوازن).

152
00:10:55,422 --> 00:10:57,650
So, he came back and told Rasool Allah ﷺ this report.

153
00:10:58,254 --> 00:11:03,750
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه didn't like what he heard, so he rejected it.

154
00:11:04,732 --> 00:11:09,827
and Abdullah Bin Abi Hazrad(عبد الله بن أبي حدرد) told him, you might be rejecting the truth.

155
00:11:10,636 --> 00:11:18,655
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ told Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) that you were once misled and Allahعَزّوجَلّ has guided you.

156
00:11:19,371 --> 00:11:24,844
Anyway, Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted additional arms, for the army.

157
00:11:25,286 --> 00:11:26,805
So, he spoke to Safwaan Ibn Ummayyah(صفوان ابن اُمَيَّة),

158
00:11:27,374 --> 00:11:31,439
Safwaan(صفوان) being one of the leaders of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), and one of the wealthy among them.

159
00:11:31,780 --> 00:11:33,882
He has a good stock pile of weapons.

160
00:11:34,446 --> 00:11:43,613
 So, Rasool Allah ﷺ asked him to give him, narrations are different, it says spears and shields.

161
00:11:44,570 --> 00:11:47,408
Safwaan(صفوان) asked Rasool Allah ﷺ;

162
00:11:47,553 --> 00:11:48,897
عَارِيَّةً اَمْ غَصْبًا؟

163
00:11:49,182 --> 00:11:51,704
Are you taking them by force or you're borrowing them.

164
00:11:52,310 --> 00:11:56,626
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him: No, I'm borrowing them and I will return them to you.

165
00:11:57,255 --> 00:12:01,598
Safwaan(صفوان) agreed and Rasool Allah ﷺ, if you want to take it by force he could.

166
00:12:01,888 --> 00:12:05,884
And keep in mind that Safwaan(صفوان) is still a Kafir(كافر) now,

167
00:12:06,411 --> 00:12:10,192
and he's a subject of the Muslim state

168
00:12:10,766 --> 00:12:16,493
and Rasool Allah ﷺ could have taken from him, the arms if he wanted

169
00:12:16,518 --> 00:12:20,817
but Rasool Allah ﷺ told him: No, I will borrow them and return them back to you.

170
00:12:21,913 --> 00:12:24,620
And Safwaan(صفوان) was still in that waiting period

171
00:12:24,700 --> 00:12:29,200
Safwaan(صفوان) asked for two months, Rasool Allah ﷺ gave him four.

172
00:12:30,039 --> 00:12:33,583
It says in some narrations, it gives the numbers but they're different.

173
00:12:33,623 --> 00:12:38,084
Anyway, after the battle some of them were lost, some of the pieces were lost.

174
00:12:38,862 --> 00:12:41,575
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ gave him what remained

175
00:12:41,954 --> 00:12:48,070
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ told him; I can pay you back, compensate you, financially for the pieces that were lost.

176
00:12:48,370 --> 00:12:50,597
Safwaan Ibn Ummayyah(صفوان ابن اميه) said: No, Don't do that.

177
00:12:50,921 --> 00:12:54,559
Because I find in my heart now, what I didn't find then.

178
00:12:54,863 --> 00:12:58,441
Now, what Safwaan(صفوان) is talking about is.? Islam.

179
00:12:58,474 --> 00:13:03,214
Now, I'm closest to Islam, I'm beginning to become closer to Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

180
00:13:03,405 --> 00:13:07,322
And he refused to take any compensation for the pieces that were lost.

181
00:13:08,716 --> 00:13:13,748
On the way the Muslims passed by a tree, a large tree

182
00:13:14,116 --> 00:13:21,169
and this tree, the Mushrikeen(مشركين) used to hang their swords on this tree to get Barakah(بركة),

183
00:13:21,840 --> 00:13:23,922
so that they will get some blessings.

184
00:13:24,269 --> 00:13:29,552
It's one of the rituals of Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة) that have no foundation, myths and superstition.

185
00:13:30,368 --> 00:13:35,058
But because the army of the Muslims included people who are new in their Islam

186
00:13:35,082 --> 00:13:38,384
and didn't have Fiqh(فقه) and didn't have understanding of the proper aqeedah(عقيده).

187
00:13:39,052 --> 00:13:41,105
They said: O Rasool Ullah;

188
00:13:41,129 --> 00:13:44,234
يَا رَسول الله، اِجْعَلْ لَنَا ذَاتَ اَنْوَاطٍ كَمَا لَهُمْ ذَاتَ اَنْوَاطِ

189
00:13:45,535 --> 00:13:51,364
O Rasool Ullah, we want to have Zaat Anwaat(ذات أنواط), like the disbelievers have Zaat Anwaat(ذات أنواط)

190
00:13:51,404 --> 00:13:56,136
just as they have a tree where they hang their swords and get blessings.

191
00:13:56,390 --> 00:13:58,039
We want to have something similar.

192
00:13:58,793 --> 00:13:59,958
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

193
00:14:00,250 --> 00:14:04,470
قُلْتُمْ وَالَّذِيْ نَفْسِ بِيَدِه، كَمَا قَالَ قَوْمُ مُوْسَى

194
00:14:04,717 --> 00:14:07,341
اَجْعَلْ لَنَا إِلَٰهًا كَمَا لَهُمْ آلِهَةٌ ۚ

195
00:14:07,576 --> 00:14:11,052
In the name of Allah whom, my soul is in His hands,

196
00:14:11,283 --> 00:14:15,838
you have said something similar to what the people of Musa(موسى) have said,

197
00:14:16,100 --> 00:14:20,812
Musa(موسى) we want to have a god as they have gods,

198
00:14:21,144 --> 00:14:25,066
because Bannu Israel(بنوإسرائيل), when they crossed the sea.

199
00:14:25,647 --> 00:14:33,861
They asked Musa(موسى) to allow them to have god's like these people, who are Musrikeen(مشركين) in front of them have gods

200
00:14:34,060 --> 00:14:36,903
and Allahعَزّوجَلّ says that Musa(موسى) told them;

201
00:14:36,935 --> 00:14:38,582
إِنَّكُمْ قَوْمٌ تَجْهَلُونَ

202
00:14:38,709 --> 00:14:40,475
You are people who are ignorant.

203
00:14:40,500 --> 00:14:41,898
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

204
00:14:42,160 --> 00:14:48,923
اِنَّهَا لَسُنَنْ، لَتَرْكَبُنَّ سُنَنَ مَنْ كَانَ قَبْلَكُمْ سُنَة سُنَّةْ

205
00:14:49,365 --> 00:14:58,280
These are the ways of the past, you will follow them one by one, in this narration, Sunnatan Sunnah (سنتن سنه)

206
00:14:58,332 --> 00:15:02,519
you will follow the ways of the disbelievers before you, one by one,

207
00:15:02,591 --> 00:15:09,632
meaning everything that the disbelievers of the nation of Musa(موسى), people of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) did,

208
00:15:09,748 --> 00:15:14,032
you will find something similar to it in this Ummah(أمة) of Muhammadﷺ.

209
00:15:14,223 --> 00:15:20,092
The difference is that the evil in the Ummah(امة) of Bannu Israel(بنو إسرائيل) was prevalent

210
00:15:20,378 --> 00:15:24,402
and it has overcome the good and became dominant.

211
00:15:24,753 --> 00:15:28,962
While with the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ, they will never ceased to be people on the truth,

212
00:15:29,351 --> 00:15:31,883
who are holding firm to the religion of Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

213
00:15:32,184 --> 00:15:36,192
and this is how the religion of Allahعَزّوجَلّ will carry on, until the Day of Judgment.

214
00:15:36,508 --> 00:15:38,370
Even if there are people who are deviant,

215
00:15:38,588 --> 00:15:43,711
even if there are people, who are following the ways of the disbelieving nations before us.

216
00:15:44,051 --> 00:15:48,808
Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted someone to guard them, this night.

217
00:15:49,530 --> 00:15:51,495
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

218
00:15:51,671 --> 00:15:52,945
مَنْ يَحْرُسْنَا اللَّيْلَةْ؟

219
00:15:53,480 --> 00:15:59,122
Who will be our guard this night, who will stand guard this night.?

220
00:15:59,825 --> 00:16:03,052
The companion, Anas Ibn Abi Marsad(أنس إبن أبي مرثد) volunteered.

221
00:16:03,955 --> 00:16:06,748
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told him, Irqab(إرقب), ride.

222
00:16:07,159 --> 00:16:09,746
So, he was on horseback.

223
00:16:10,405 --> 00:16:13,862
He came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;

224
00:16:13,886 --> 00:16:19,555
اِسْتَقْبِلْ هَذَا الشَّعْب حَتَّى تَكُوْنَ فِيْ اَعْلَاهْ وَلَا نُغَرَّنَّ مِنْ قِبِلِكَ اللَّيْلَةْ

225
00:16:20,497 --> 00:16:26,521
He said: Face this valley or mountain pass, until you reach to the end of it.

226
00:16:26,884 --> 00:16:28,356
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;

227
00:16:28,587 --> 00:16:33,486
and we don't want to be taken by surprise from your direction.

228
00:16:33,834 --> 00:16:37,949
This is your responsibility. This is your part. This is your duty.

229
00:16:38,243 --> 00:16:41,241
We do not want to be attacked from your part.

230
00:16:41,550 --> 00:16:44,330
We do not want to be taken by surprise from your part.

231
00:16:44,998 --> 00:16:46,999
This should be the duty of every Muslim,

232
00:16:47,785 --> 00:16:54,812
every Muslim should be protecting Islam from his direction, from his end

233
00:16:55,049 --> 00:16:58,274
 and we should not allow Islam to be attacked from our end.

234
00:16:58,723 --> 00:17:00,763
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him,

235
00:17:00,892 --> 00:17:05,851
that we do not want to be surprised by an attack from your end, this evening.

236
00:17:06,179 --> 00:17:10,481
In the morning, this narration is in Sunnan Abi Dawood(سنن أبي داؤد).

237
00:17:11,329 --> 00:17:15,862
فَلَمَّا اَصْبَحْنَا خَرَجَ رَسُوْلَ الله صلى الله عليه وسلم اِلَى مُصَلَّاهْ

238
00:17:16,217 --> 00:17:20,682
Rasool Allah ﷺ went to the Mussallah(مصلى), the place, where they're going to pray Fajar(فجر)

239
00:17:20,912 --> 00:17:22,141
فَرَكَعَةْ رَكَعْتَيْنَ

240
00:17:22,474 --> 00:17:24,573
 So, he prayed two Raka'h(ركعة) and then he said;

241
00:17:24,726 --> 00:17:26,463
هَلْ اَحْسَسْتُمْ فَارِسَكُمْ؟

242
00:17:26,788 --> 00:17:33,588
Did you feel your knight meaning, did you see him or hear his movement.

243
00:17:33,810 --> 00:17:35,282
قَالُوْ يا رسول الله ، مَا اَحْسَسْنَا

244
00:17:35,322 --> 00:17:36,346
They said: O Rasool Ullah, No.

245
00:17:36,788 --> 00:17:41,103
فَثُوْبَ بِالصَّلَاةْ فَجَعَلَ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يُصَلِّيْ

246
00:17:41,128 --> 00:17:43,598
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ started Salat Ul Fajar(صلاة الفجر),

247
00:17:43,622 --> 00:17:47,201
so first he prayed the Sunnah Fajar(سنة فجر) and now they're praying the Salah(صلاة) of Fajar(فجر)

248
00:17:47,775 --> 00:17:49,666
while Rasool Allah ﷺ was in Salah(صلاة)

249
00:17:50,631 --> 00:17:52,064
وَهُوَ يَلْتَفِت اِلَى الشِّعْبَ

250
00:17:52,599 --> 00:17:59,779
And while Rasool Allah ﷺ was praying he was looking towards the direction of the valley.

251
00:18:00,280 --> 00:18:02,200
حَتَّى اِذَا قَضَى صَلَاتَه’

252
00:18:02,224 --> 00:18:03,910
And when he finished his prayer.

253
00:18:04,327 --> 00:18:08,021
وَسَلَّمَا قَالَ: اَبْشِرُوْا فَقَدْ جَاءَكُمْ فَارِسُكُمْ

254
00:18:08,258 --> 00:18:14,294
And when he gave Salam(سلام), he said: Bear the glad tidings your knight has arrived.

255
00:18:14,319 --> 00:18:16,939
فَجَعَلْنَا نَنْظِرُ اِلَى خِلَالِ الشَّجَرْ

256
00:18:17,209 --> 00:18:21,135
And we kept on staring towards the trees and we couldn't see anything.

257
00:18:21,160 --> 00:18:23,200
So Rasool Allah ﷺ saw him before anybody else.

258
00:18:23,523 --> 00:18:27,974
And then he told them that the knight is coming and they were still looking but didn't see him

259
00:18:28,167 --> 00:18:34,190
and then after that they saw his movement between the trees on his horse back.

260
00:18:34,214 --> 00:18:37,369
وَاِذَا هُوَ قَدْ جَاءْ حَتَى وَقَفَ عَلَى رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم

261
00:18:37,393 --> 00:18:41,729
And then he came, and came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and he gave him Salaam(سلام).

262
00:18:41,753 --> 00:18:44,681
تَسَلَمَّ فَقَال: اِنِّيْ اَنْطَلَقْتُ حَتَّى كُنْتَ

263
00:18:44,876 --> 00:18:48,246
فِيْ اَعْلَى هَذَاالشِّعْب حَيْثُ اَمَرَنِيْ رَسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم

264
00:18:48,310 --> 00:18:51,960
I was in the place, where you have given me instructions to be.

265
00:18:52,049 --> 00:18:55,959
فَلَمَّا اَصْبَحَت طَلَعَت الشِّعْبَيْنَ كِلَيْهِمَا

266
00:18:56,081 --> 00:19:02,137
And when it was morning, I looked from top of the two mountains and I didn't see anyone.

267
00:19:02,168 --> 00:19:06,257
فَنَظَرْتُ فَلَمْ أَرَ أَحَداً‏،فَقَالَ لَه’ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم‏:‏ ‏هَلْ نَزَلْتُ اللَّيْلَةْ ‏؟‏‏‏‏

268
00:19:06,609 --> 00:19:09,141
Did you descend at all this evening?

269
00:19:09,497 --> 00:19:12,728
قَالَ‏:‏ لَا، إِلَّا مُصَلِّياً أَوْ قَاضَيا حَاجَةً‏

270
00:19:12,752 --> 00:19:19,767
No, except if it was for prayer, or to respond to the call of nature to relieve myself.

271
00:19:20,146 --> 00:19:22,405
فَقَالَ لَه’ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم‏

272
00:19:22,666 --> 00:19:23,781
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him.

273
00:19:23,805 --> 00:19:26,993
‏قَدْ أَوْجَبْت فَلَا عَلَيْكَ أَلَّا تَعْمَلَ بَعْدَهَا

274
00:19:27,286 --> 00:19:31,080
Aoujabat(أوجبت) meaning that Allahعَزّوجَلّ will grant you Jannah(جنة),

275
00:19:31,104 --> 00:19:32,803
فَلَا عَلَيْكَ أَلَّا تَعْمَلَ بَعْدَهَا

276
00:19:32,927 --> 00:19:34,823
You do not have to do anything after this.

277
00:19:35,513 --> 00:19:40,423
So, the guarding of Anas Ibn Abi Marsad(انس ابن ابي مرثد),

278
00:19:40,981 --> 00:19:47,723
and fulfilling his duty as described by Rasool Allah ﷺ is an act that granted him Jannah(جنة).

279
00:19:47,984 --> 00:19:53,032
And this reveals to us the great reward of guarding Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله),

280
00:19:53,396 --> 00:19:59,033
standing guard for the armies of the fighters, Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

281
00:19:59,416 --> 00:20:07,757
This is a great reward that Rasool Allah ﷺ has promised the companion Anas Ibn Abi Marsad رضي الله عنه.

282
00:20:08,353 --> 00:20:11,829
It was a very hot day, Abu Abdur Rahman Al-Fahri(أبو عبدالرحمن ألفهري) said;

283
00:20:11,853 --> 00:20:14,373
فَسِرنَّا فِيْ يَوْمٍ كَائِذٍ شَدِيْدِ الْحَرْبَ

284
00:20:15,010 --> 00:20:19,962
Let's look at the climate on the battlefield, it was a very hot day.

285
00:20:20,419 --> 00:20:25,635
And this heat causes exhaustion and it affects the fighter,

286
00:20:26,022 --> 00:20:30,473
see the difficulty that was involved in this battle.

287
00:20:30,777 --> 00:20:32,755
So, it started out as a hot day.

288
00:20:33,454 --> 00:20:37,709
They took a nap under whatever trees they could find.

289
00:20:38,252 --> 00:20:45,222
And Rasool Allah ﷺ called Bilal(بلال) and says that Bilal(بلال) stood up from beneath a tree

290
00:20:45,246 --> 00:20:47,378
ظِلُّهَا كَظِلِّ طَائِرْ

291
00:20:47,655 --> 00:20:52,244
And the shade that, this tree would offer is like the shade of a bird.

292
00:20:52,327 --> 00:20:53,807
The shade is useless.

293
00:20:54,116 --> 00:20:59,322
 But this was the climate that they had on that day.

294
00:20:59,589 --> 00:21:03,339
They started marching in this mountainous terrain.

295
00:21:04,080 --> 00:21:06,467
So, it's hot, and it's rough, mountainous terrain,

296
00:21:06,774 --> 00:21:13,753
and they were suddenly shocked by the attack of the horsemen of Hawazin(هوازن) from in front,

297
00:21:13,889 --> 00:21:19,090
and then they were attacked by the archers of Hawazin(هوازن) from the sides.

298
00:21:19,881 --> 00:21:21,946
And it says in the books of Seerah(سيرة).

299
00:21:21,970 --> 00:21:23,275
وَكَانُوْ قَوْمَ الرُّمَا

300
00:21:23,806 --> 00:21:26,737
It says that the people of Hawazin(هوازن) were good archers,

301
00:21:27,609 --> 00:21:32,134
and the arrows were falling on the Muslims from each direction.

302
00:21:32,863 --> 00:21:35,746
And the horses were attacking from the front.

303
00:21:36,170 --> 00:21:39,625
So, the Muslims were caught by surprise.

304
00:21:40,077 --> 00:21:44,817
The front of the army was Bannu Sulaim(بنوسُلَيْم) a tribe next to Madina.

305
00:21:45,354 --> 00:21:47,755
They retreated they couldn't handle the shock.

306
00:21:48,668 --> 00:21:51,703
So, they started fleeing from the battlefield.

307
00:21:52,003 --> 00:21:55,204
And then behind them was At-Tulaqa'a(ألطلاقآء).

308
00:21:55,613 --> 00:21:59,687
The ones, who were released, and these were new in Islam,

309
00:21:59,962 --> 00:22:03,107
their Tawaqul(توكل) and Yaqeen(يقين) in Allahعَزّوجَلّ was weak.

310
00:22:03,311 --> 00:22:07,027
So, they also retreated and their number was large about 2000.

311
00:22:08,005 --> 00:22:10,489
And then it says, in the narration;

312
00:22:10,807 --> 00:22:13,117
فَرَكِبَتِ الْاِبِلْ بَعْضَهَا الْبَعْضْ

313
00:22:13,868 --> 00:22:19,415
Camels were Stumbling on one another, so it was a chaotic stage.

314
00:22:20,179 --> 00:22:24,731
camels were crowded, and they were stumbling and stepping over one another.

315
00:22:24,930 --> 00:22:28,178
So, the alignment of the army was gone.

316
00:22:28,446 --> 00:22:34,399
The organizing of the different battalions was gone and it was a chaotic state.

317
00:22:34,694 --> 00:22:39,347
You have the two groups, who are in the front, they were already fleeing away from their positions.

318
00:22:39,645 --> 00:22:44,993
And then chaos ensued with the rest of the army and now everybody was fleeing away.

319
00:22:45,757 --> 00:22:48,994
Rasool Allah ﷺ was calling them and saying;

320
00:22:49,019 --> 00:22:50,188
أَيْنَ أَيُّهَا النَّاسْ

321
00:22:50,220 --> 00:22:51,530
Where to, O people.!

322
00:22:51,826 --> 00:22:52,834
هَلُمُّوْا إِلَيْ،

323
00:22:52,858 --> 00:22:53,823
Come to me!

324
00:22:54,048 --> 00:22:57,328
أَنَا رسول الله، أَنَا رسول الله، أَنَا محمد بن عبد الله،

325
00:22:57,510 --> 00:23:00,623
I am the messenger of Allah, I am the messenger of Allah!

326
00:23:00,647 --> 00:23:02,410
I am Muhammad(محمد), the son of Abdullah(عبدالله).

327
00:23:02,678 --> 00:23:04,989
The narrator of the Hadith(حديث), Jabir Bin Abdullah(جابر بن عبدالله) says;

328
00:23:05,029 --> 00:23:05,736
فَلَا شَيْء

329
00:23:05,935 --> 00:23:08,255
Rasool Allah ﷺ is calling them to no avail.

330
00:23:08,834 --> 00:23:10,190
They're running away.

331
00:23:10,642 --> 00:23:13,332
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان); When he saw this, he said;

332
00:23:13,356 --> 00:23:15,304
وَللهِ لَا تَنْتَهِيْ هَزِيْمَتُهُمْ اِلَّا فِيْ البَحْر

333
00:23:16,254 --> 00:23:19,850
The defeat will not end, except at the sea.

334
00:23:20,113 --> 00:23:23,443
Meaning they're going to carry on running, until they reach to the sea.

335
00:23:24,219 --> 00:23:28,327
And Kalda Ibn Hanbal(كلده إبن حنبل), he said;

336
00:23:28,488 --> 00:23:29,716
بَطُلَ السَّحْر

337
00:23:29,920 --> 00:23:36,717
The magic is gone, that's it, the magic of Muhammadﷺ worked until this day but now it's not working anymore.

338
00:23:36,757 --> 00:23:38,535
 That's it! This is the end of magic!

339
00:23:39,268 --> 00:23:45,668
You see how these people, who are new in Islam when they saw what was happening,

340
00:23:46,027 --> 00:23:49,224
they lost their trust, in the truth.

341
00:23:49,662 --> 00:23:53,403
And that's it they saw that the Muslims are defeated and there's no use.

342
00:23:53,702 --> 00:23:58,264
Safwaan(صفوان) however, he didn't like what he heard, he wasn't happy with it.

343
00:23:58,705 --> 00:24:04,383
And he said: I would rather have a man from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) rule over me than a Bedouin from Hawazin(هوازن).

344
00:24:04,735 --> 00:24:08,121
So Ya'ni(يعني) even though his intentions were not for the Haqq(حق) but,

345
00:24:08,376 --> 00:24:11,316
even though it was out of tribalism and nationalism,

346
00:24:11,356 --> 00:24:16,031
but he's still had a better position than Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) and Kalda Ibn Hanbal(كلده إبن حنبل).

347
00:24:16,869 --> 00:24:19,226
When he criticized them for their words and said;

348
00:24:19,266 --> 00:24:23,457
I would rather have Rasool Allah ﷺ win then have a Bedouin rule over me.

349
00:24:23,804 --> 00:24:30,421
So, you can see there was some background sensitivity between the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and the people of Thaqeef(ثقيف) or Hawazin(هوازن).

350
00:24:30,601 --> 00:24:34,675
Salamah Ibn Akwa رضي الله عنه, narrates and this is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

351
00:24:34,903 --> 00:24:39,408
He said: When the retreat started, I was fleeing.

352
00:24:39,772 --> 00:24:42,106
And who is this? This is Salamah Ibn Aqwa(سلمه ابن اكوع).

353
00:24:42,166 --> 00:24:44,952
Remember the heroic stories of Salamah Ibn Aqwa(سلمه ابن اكوع)?

354
00:24:45,414 --> 00:24:47,597
We talked about him more than once.

355
00:24:47,947 --> 00:24:52,672
We talked about the story of Zooqarad(ذو قرد) when he fought the Mushrikeen(مشركين) alone.

356
00:24:53,071 --> 00:24:55,917
We talked about the praise that Rasool Allah ﷺ praised him

357
00:24:56,389 --> 00:25:00,784
that the best of our fighters on foot is Salamah Ibn Aqwa(سلمه بن اكوع).

358
00:25:01,330 --> 00:25:05,289
So, we're not talking about somebody who was, who was weak or he's not a good fighter.

359
00:25:05,313 --> 00:25:06,916
We're talking about one of the best fighters

360
00:25:07,255 --> 00:25:11,128
Salamah Ibn Aqwa رضي الله عنه said: I was fleeing

361
00:25:11,391 --> 00:25:18,141
and I had to garments on me and they were untied, so than I tied them together and began running.

362
00:25:19,136 --> 00:25:22,431
He said: When I passed next to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

363
00:25:22,538 --> 00:25:24,540
Rasool Allah ﷺ when he saw me, he said;

364
00:25:24,565 --> 00:25:26,936
لَقَدْ رَاَى اِبْنَ الاَكْوَع ذعرا

365
00:25:27,399 --> 00:25:30,693
Look, The son of Al-Akwah(ألْأكوع) has seen something terrifying.

366
00:25:30,717 --> 00:25:32,691
When Rasool Allah ﷺ saw the face of Salamah(سلمه).

367
00:25:33,224 --> 00:25:34,944
And saw, the way he's running.

368
00:25:35,442 --> 00:25:38,927
Rasool Allah ﷺ said that, he has saw something that is terrifying.

369
00:25:39,182 --> 00:25:42,409
So, the situation was dire, the situation was difficult.

370
00:25:42,802 --> 00:25:47,603
But even though the situation was difficult,

371
00:25:48,127 --> 00:25:55,230
Even though the world around you, not just the battlefield, the entire world around you, could be in a mess.

372
00:25:56,102 --> 00:26:02,358
But Allahعَزّوجَلّ can give you Sakeena(سكينه), tranquility, and can give you a peace in your heart.

373
00:26:02,866 --> 00:26:06,266
 Even in difficult times, like these.

374
00:26:06,472 --> 00:26:12,272
While on the other hand, things could be great around you, things could be peaceful.

375
00:26:13,040 --> 00:26:22,764
Nevertheless, Allahعَزّوجَلّ puts in the heart, the exact opposite feeling, feeling of despair, feeling of depression.

376
00:26:23,178 --> 00:26:27,162
 So, one cannot judge the affairs by the outside.

377
00:26:27,452 --> 00:26:31,375
But the judgment is based on what is inside, what is in the hearts.

378
00:26:31,933 --> 00:26:39,518
Dear brothers and sisters, if we follow the rule of Allahعَزّوجَلّ, even though we might go through moments of difficulty,

379
00:26:39,594 --> 00:26:43,437
but Allahسبحانه وتعالى promised us that after difficulty there's ease.

380
00:26:44,115 --> 00:26:46,640
فَإِنَّ مَعَ الْعُسْرِ يُسْرًا َإِنَّ مَعَ الْعُسْرِ يُسْرًا َ

381
00:26:47,034 --> 00:26:52,438
With difficulty comes ease, with difficulty comes ease, it's a promise from Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

382
00:26:52,623 --> 00:26:54,000
And that's why in the Battle of Badr(بدر),

383
00:26:54,394 --> 00:26:57,776
which was the first meeting between the Kuffar(كفار) and the Muslims,

384
00:26:58,187 --> 00:26:59,618
it was a moment of difficulty

385
00:27:00,201 --> 00:27:04,699
it was a very difficult moment for the Muslims, they don't know what the outcome would be.

386
00:27:05,469 --> 00:27:07,449
But what they see with their eyes is that

387
00:27:07,501 --> 00:27:15,414
they're facing an adversary, who is more in numbers and better in preparation and better armed and they were few

388
00:27:16,358 --> 00:27:22,760
In that difficult time even though there was some difficult feelings in the heart.

389
00:27:22,947 --> 00:27:25,169
Nevertheless, Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

390
00:27:25,534 --> 00:27:36,534
And then slumber came to them, they slept they felt this feeling of drowsiness, and sleeping in this difficult time.

391
00:27:37,056 --> 00:27:40,616
And here in the Battle of Hunain(حنين), Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

392
00:27:40,647 --> 00:27:42,787
 Even though we talked about the situation of Salamah(سلمه),

393
00:27:42,999 --> 00:27:49,139
and we said that Rasool Allah ﷺ was calling the people and and no one was responding, everybody was running away, after this.

394
00:27:49,451 --> 00:27:52,908
After this difficulty what happened Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

395
00:27:53,085 --> 00:28:01,308
ثُمَّ أَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ سَكِينَتَهُ عَلَىٰ رَسُولِهِ وَعَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ

396
00:28:01,656 --> 00:28:08,347
وَأَنْزَلَ جُنُودًا لَمْ تَرَوْهَا وَعَذَّبَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا ۚ

397
00:28:08,548 --> 00:28:14,228
وَذَٰلِكَ جَزَاءُ الْكَافِرِين۝

398
00:28:14,571 --> 00:28:21,523
Allahعَزّوجَلّ, revealed tranquility on the messenger, and on the believers,

399
00:28:21,793 --> 00:28:25,722
and he supported them with soldiers that you did not see.

400
00:28:26,430 --> 00:28:28,767
What are the soldiers of Allah.? Angels!

401
00:28:28,996 --> 00:28:34,998
There's one narration, it says, that we saw a black cloud falling from the sky.

402
00:28:35,366 --> 00:28:42,256
And then when it landed on the ground, we saw numerous ants, it was like a carpet of ants.

403
00:28:42,609 --> 00:28:46,218
And we thought that, these were the angels that came from Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

404
00:28:46,243 --> 00:28:49,118
Allah Ho Aalam(الله اعلم) how authentic this might be.

405
00:28:49,391 --> 00:28:54,560
The Ayah(آية) could mean this or it could mean, carry a different meaning.

406
00:28:54,872 --> 00:28:59,849
But regardless Allahعَزّوجَلّ says that He has provided them with soldiers.

407
00:29:00,226 --> 00:29:07,614
And this changed the situation and it changed it in a way that was unimaginable

408
00:29:07,638 --> 00:29:12,505
because we have seen what Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) said, and what Kulda Bin Hanbal(كلده بن حنبل) said

409
00:29:12,798 --> 00:29:18,061
and we have seen the response of the Sahabah(صحابه), whom most of them retreated,

410
00:29:18,403 --> 00:29:21,288
and only a small number remained with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

411
00:29:21,328 --> 00:29:27,050
Initially, it was only a few, it was Al-Abbas Bin Abdul Muttalib(العباس بن عبدالمطلب) and Abu Sufiyan Ibn Haris(ابو سفيان ابن حارث),

412
00:29:27,426 --> 00:29:30,842
and one of the sons of Al-Abbas Bin Abdul Muttalib(العباس بن عبدالمطلب),

413
00:29:31,106 --> 00:29:36,476
and Aimen(ايمن), the son of Umm Aiman(ام ايمن), who was the nurse of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

414
00:29:36,904 --> 00:29:42,904
Only these were surrounding Rasool Allah ﷺ, and holding on to his mule,

415
00:29:42,929 --> 00:29:45,986
the rest have fled from their location.

416
00:29:46,909 --> 00:29:53,263
At this particular moment Rasool Allah ﷺ told Al-Abbas(العباس) because his voice was very powerful.

417
00:29:53,532 --> 00:29:56,538
Rasool Allah ﷺ, told him to call Al-Ansar(الانصار).

418
00:29:57,479 --> 00:30:00,626
So, Al-Abbas Bin Abdul Muttalib(العباس بن عبدالمطلب) made his call to Al-Ansar(الانصار).

419
00:30:01,184 --> 00:30:04,254
And then Rasool Ullah told him to specify Al-Khazraj(ألخزرج).

420
00:30:04,752 --> 00:30:09,384
So, he called Al-Khazraj(ألخزرج) and Al-Khazraj(ألخزرج) were special fighters.

421
00:30:09,408 --> 00:30:11,094
They were strong, powerful.

422
00:30:11,645 --> 00:30:19,019
So, it says in the narration that they turned around like cows with turn around to their calves,

423
00:30:19,571 --> 00:30:23,190
and Rasool Allah ﷺ was surrounded by about a 100 men.

424
00:30:23,844 --> 00:30:27,361
These hundred men stood in front of an army.

425
00:30:27,815 --> 00:30:36,083
In which some narrations, the number is given at 40,000 strong and in another narration 20.

426
00:30:36,624 --> 00:30:38,937
Anyway, the number was huge.

427
00:30:39,175 --> 00:30:44,699
100 standing in the face of an army, that size.

428
00:30:44,940 --> 00:30:48,561
Rasool Allah ﷺ was marching ahead,

429
00:30:49,069 --> 00:30:53,453
 Rasool Allah ﷺ alone marching ahead.

430
00:30:54,058 --> 00:30:58,308
And Al-Abbas(العباس) says that we were pulling his mule to slow him down.

431
00:30:58,980 --> 00:31:01,782
Rasool Allah ﷺ facing this army of the enemy.

432
00:31:02,054 --> 00:31:08,745
It says that in the front of the army of the enemy, there was one man from Hawazin(هوازن), carrying a very long spear.

433
00:31:09,285 --> 00:31:11,527
 And on the top of the spear, there was a banner.

434
00:31:12,187 --> 00:31:18,787
If he is a head, his spear would be used to stab at the Muslims.

435
00:31:19,253 --> 00:31:26,080
And if his companions reach to him, then he would raise it up as a banner.

436
00:31:26,439 --> 00:31:35,411
So, this front of the army, the first row of the army of Hawazin(هوازن), was crushing the Muslim army,

437
00:31:35,668 --> 00:31:38,307
it was just rolling over them.

438
00:31:38,805 --> 00:31:41,945
And Rasool Allah ﷺ is now facing them alone.

439
00:31:42,484 --> 00:31:45,897
And Al-Abbas(العباس) is saying that we're trying to pull back his mule.

440
00:31:46,604 --> 00:31:50,694
Until, Rasool Allah ﷺ had the number around him between 80 and 100.

441
00:31:51,329 --> 00:31:53,655
And this is when the real fighting started,

442
00:31:53,679 --> 00:31:56,109
because in the beginning, there was no fighting.

443
00:31:56,493 --> 00:32:02,079
It was an initial shock that caused Bannu Sulaim(بنو سُلَيم) to flee and then followed by Tulaqa'a(طلقاء) and everybody else

444
00:32:02,761 --> 00:32:07,016
 and they were being slammed by arrows from every direction.

445
00:32:07,738 --> 00:32:12,130
But now the real fighting, fighting of the sword began.

446
00:32:12,495 --> 00:32:13,638
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

447
00:32:13,662 --> 00:32:15,344
اَلْآنَ حَمْيَ الْوَطِيْسْ

448
00:32:15,555 --> 00:32:19,473
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Now, the fire of battle is waging.

449
00:32:19,927 --> 00:32:22,771
This is when the fire is becoming hot.

450
00:32:23,864 --> 00:32:27,881
Rasool Allah ﷺ stood in the stirrups and started making Dua(دعا)

451
00:32:28,368 --> 00:32:33,487
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ took with his blessed hand, a handful of dirt,

452
00:32:34,105 --> 00:32:39,064
and he threw it in the air towards the direction of Hawazin(هوازن) and said;

453
00:32:39,104 --> 00:32:40,152
شَاهَتِ الْوُجُوْهْ

454
00:32:41,020 --> 00:32:47,766
This handful of dirt which was in the hands of Rasool Allah ﷺ was a soldier of Allah

455
00:32:48,557 --> 00:32:56,796
because one narration says, that every enemy fighter felt something in his eyes.

456
00:32:57,537 --> 00:33:00,222
And they also had the feeling in their hearts.

457
00:33:00,850 --> 00:33:06,395
One of them, who later became Muslim, would describe the feeling that, they had.

458
00:33:06,901 --> 00:33:11,413
When Rasool Allah ﷺ threw this single handful of dirt towards them.

459
00:33:11,686 --> 00:33:15,225
When he was asked what happened, how did you feel?

460
00:33:15,456 --> 00:33:22,828
He would take rocks and throw them in an iron pan and you would hear all of that clattering sound.

461
00:33:23,421 --> 00:33:26,790
And he would tell them; This is how we felt in our insides.

462
00:33:27,428 --> 00:33:34,423
This shaking, this crack clattering sound, this terror, is what we felt in our insides.

463
00:33:35,146 --> 00:33:41,218
We'll read this Hadith(حديث) in Musnad Imam Ahmad(مسند إمام أحمد) that gives a brief description.

464
00:33:42,345 --> 00:33:47,435
Imam Ahmad(امام احمد) stated that it was related to him, by Affan(عفان) quoting Abdul wahid Bin Ziyad(عبد الواحد بن زياد)

465
00:33:47,990 --> 00:33:54,743
quoting Al-Haris Bin Hussain(ألحارث بن حسين) quoting Al-Qasim Bin Abdur Rahman Bin Abdullah Bin Masood(ألقاسم بن عبد الرحمن بن عبدالله بن مسعود) from his father,

466
00:33:55,179 --> 00:33:57,176
who quoted Abdullah Bin Masood(عبد الله بن مسعود) as stating,

467
00:33:58,333 --> 00:34:01,908
I was present with the Messenger of Allah at the Battle of Hunain(حنين).

468
00:34:02,736 --> 00:34:04,303
The men retreated from him,

469
00:34:04,905 --> 00:34:08,974
and 80 of the Ansaar(أنْصَار) and the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) remained there with him.

470
00:34:09,438 --> 00:34:14,921
We drew back some 80 feet, but we did not turn our backs to the enemy.

471
00:34:15,532 --> 00:34:21,101
These men were the ones upon whom Allah sent down His Sakeena(سكينه), tranquility.

472
00:34:21,909 --> 00:34:27,675
The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was mean while still going forward on his mule,

473
00:34:28,050 --> 00:34:32,293
which veered to one side, so that he slipped off his saddle.

474
00:34:32,591 --> 00:34:36,443
I called out to him, up you get, may Allah raise you up?

475
00:34:36,467 --> 00:34:39,279
He replied, get me a handful of dirt.

476
00:34:40,090 --> 00:34:44,416
With this, He struck them in their faces and fill their mouths.

477
00:34:44,897 --> 00:34:48,497
Then he asked: Where are the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) and the Ansaar(أنْصَار)?

478
00:34:48,960 --> 00:34:52,125
They are close by, I replied, call for them. He said;

479
00:34:52,458 --> 00:34:58,298
I did this and they came their swords in their right hands shining like stars,

480
00:34:58,727 --> 00:35:02,476
and then the Mushrikeen(مشركين) turned their backs in retreat.

481
00:35:02,922 --> 00:35:09,768
This is the description Abdullah Bin Masood رضي الله عنه gave of the Battle of Hunain(حنين).

482
00:35:10,486 --> 00:35:14,599
Some events that occurred during the Battle of Hunain(حنين).

483
00:35:15,194 --> 00:35:16,794
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

484
00:35:17,136 --> 00:35:19,902
مَنْ قَتَلَ قَتِيْلًا فَلَه’ سَلْبُه’

485
00:35:20,367 --> 00:35:26,733
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Whoever kills an enemy gets his possessions,

486
00:35:27,447 --> 00:35:34,478
And this narration is in Bukhari(بخاري), And other books of Hadith(حديث) also

487
00:35:35,349 --> 00:35:40,048
Abu Qatadah(ابو قتادة) says; that, there was one of Al-Mushrikeen(ألمشركين),

488
00:35:40,552 --> 00:35:43,906
who raised his hand to strike a Muslim.

489
00:35:44,582 --> 00:35:48,541
So, I came from behind him and struck him with my sword on his shoulder

490
00:35:48,928 --> 00:35:51,766
until, my sword dug deep into the armor.

491
00:35:52,137 --> 00:35:57,440
So, the blow was strong enough to break through the armor and dig into his shoulder.

492
00:35:58,109 --> 00:36:03,788
So, the man turned around and embraced me, (He embraced him so hard).

493
00:36:04,058 --> 00:36:08,201
Abu Qatadah(ابو قتادة) said: I felt death, he was almost going to die

494
00:36:08,440 --> 00:36:11,882
because of the powerful, embrace of this man.

495
00:36:12,490 --> 00:36:14,178
But then, he fell down dead.

496
00:36:15,104 --> 00:36:21,047
And then the retreat occurred, and I was among those, who were retreating.

497
00:36:21,356 --> 00:36:24,116
I saw Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), I told him what is happening,

498
00:36:24,338 --> 00:36:27,178
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said; This is the decree of Allah, Amrullah(أمر الله).

499
00:36:27,432 --> 00:36:29,191
This is the decree of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

500
00:36:29,860 --> 00:36:35,329
When Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Whoever kills someone, then his possessions belong to him.

501
00:36:35,850 --> 00:36:39,807
Abu Qatadah(ابو قتادة) was searching for somebody to witness for him,

502
00:36:39,832 --> 00:36:41,470
that he's the one who killed this man.

503
00:36:42,289 --> 00:36:43,287
So, he stood up and said;

504
00:36:43,327 --> 00:36:44,137
مَنْ يَشْهَدْلِيْ

505
00:36:44,262 --> 00:36:47,576
Nobody gave witness for him, he did it again.

506
00:36:47,601 --> 00:36:48,505
 مَنْ يَشْهَدْلِيْ

507
00:36:49,004 --> 00:36:52,062
No one stood up, he did it the third time.

508
00:36:52,087 --> 00:36:52,918
 مَنْ يَشْهَدْلِيْ

509
00:36:53,276 --> 00:36:56,416
Who will witness for me, nobody gave witness

510
00:36:56,943 --> 00:37:00,785
and then one man from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) stood up and said;

511
00:37:01,158 --> 00:37:06,676
O Rasool Ullah, I am the one who took the possessions of that man, who was killed.

512
00:37:07,079 --> 00:37:12,124
So, ask Abu Qatadah(ابوقتادة) to allow me to have them.

513
00:37:13,056 --> 00:37:16,285
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه interfered, and he said;

514
00:37:16,648 --> 00:37:17,070
No!

515
00:37:17,110 --> 00:37:25,232
In the name of Allah, we're not gonna have a lion from among the lions of Allah, have nothing,

516
00:37:25,764 --> 00:37:29,074
 and given it to a hyena from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

517
00:37:30,078 --> 00:37:35,497
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is talking about Abu Qatadah(ابوقتادة) and describing him as being a lion

518
00:37:36,051 --> 00:37:37,701
and Abu Qatadah(ابوقتادة) is a lion

519
00:37:38,225 --> 00:37:44,092
 and we've talked about Abu Qatadah(ابوقتادة), we talked about some of the incidents that relate to Abu Qatadah رضي الله عنه.

520
00:37:44,117 --> 00:37:48,385
One of the fighters among As-Sahabah رضي الله عنهم Ajmaeen(اجمعين).

521
00:37:49,186 --> 00:37:56,105
So, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) did not want Abu Qatadah(ابو قتادة) to lose his possessions, for the sake of who?

522
00:37:56,402 --> 00:37:59,562
For the sake of a man, who probably just became Muslim from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

523
00:37:59,586 --> 00:38:01,981
and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) called him a hyena.

524
00:38:02,353 --> 00:38:07,445
You can see the comparison between the lion and a hyena.

525
00:38:08,347 --> 00:38:12,367
And eventually Abu Qatadah(ابوقتادة) took his possessions

526
00:38:12,596 --> 00:38:16,277
because Rasool Allah ﷺ told him: Aatiyhee(أعطيه) give him, that belongs to him.

527
00:38:16,708 --> 00:38:19,916
Abu Qatadah(ابوقتادة) said: I took those possessions and I sold them.

528
00:38:20,623 --> 00:38:25,471
And I bought with them a small number of date palms.

529
00:38:26,022 --> 00:38:30,969
And he said: This was the first wealth, I owned in Islam.

530
00:38:31,278 --> 00:38:36,975
This is the first property that I owned in Islam.

531
00:38:37,021 --> 00:38:38,947
So Abu Qatadah(ابوقتادة) had nothing

532
00:38:39,256 --> 00:38:47,054
and the first possession or property that he owned came to him from Ghaneemah Fee-Sabeelillah(غنيمه في سبيل الله).

533
00:38:47,830 --> 00:38:52,709
Next Abu Talha(ابوطلحه) saw his wife, Umm Sulaim(ام سُلَيْمْ) carrying a dagger.

534
00:38:53,135 --> 00:38:54,331
He told her, what is this?

535
00:38:54,796 --> 00:38:59,664
She said: I'm gonna rip open stomach of any of the Kuffar(كفار), who comes next to me.

536
00:38:59,965 --> 00:39:03,626
Abu Talha(ابوطلحه) said: O Rasool Ullah, Did you hear what she said?

537
00:39:03,857 --> 00:39:06,382
Rasool Allah ﷺ laughed and then she said;

538
00:39:06,737 --> 00:39:10,909
يا رسول الله: اُقْتُلْ مِن بَعَدَنَا مِنَّ الطُلَقَاءِ انهَزَمُوا بِك

539
00:39:10,934 --> 00:39:16,856
O Rasool Ullah kill all of those released ones, they were the reason of our defeat.

540
00:39:17,625 --> 00:39:21,730
She's talking about these new Muslims, who came from Makkah in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

541
00:39:22,164 --> 00:39:23,232
Rasool Allah ﷺ told her;

542
00:39:23,257 --> 00:39:25,169
اِنَّ الله قَدْ كَفَى وَاَحْسَنْ

543
00:39:25,580 --> 00:39:32,363
Allahعَزّوجَلّ has taken care of us and he has done us good, we don't need to kill anyone.

544
00:39:32,493 --> 00:39:36,075
Al-Hamdolillah(ألحمدالله) we have achieved victory, there is no need to do that.

545
00:39:36,579 --> 00:39:41,039
In this incident you can see an example of the Sahabiaat(صحابيات),

546
00:39:41,063 --> 00:39:44,532
and an example of one of the women of Al-Ansaar رضي الله عنها.

547
00:39:45,013 --> 00:39:48,982
Next there was a group of men gathering around something,

548
00:39:49,064 --> 00:39:51,624
 so Rasool Allah ﷺ asked; What was it?

549
00:39:52,212 --> 00:39:56,380
And he was told that it's a woman who was killed by Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد).

550
00:39:57,032 --> 00:39:58,348
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

551
00:39:58,372 --> 00:40:00,020
مَا كَانَتْ هَذِه لِتُقَاتِلْ

552
00:40:00,539 --> 00:40:05,313
This woman is not a combat, she was not fighting.

553
00:40:05,880 --> 00:40:11,694
And Rasool Allah ﷺ gave instructions, to tell Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) not to kill women,

554
00:40:12,061 --> 00:40:13,988
وَلَا عَسِيْفًا وَلَا ذُرِّيَّة

555
00:40:14,375 --> 00:40:19,744
And not to kill the labors, and not to kill the children.

556
00:40:20,701 --> 00:40:23,873
And this is referring to intentionally killing them.

557
00:40:24,494 --> 00:40:31,964
We'll close with the Ayah(آية) that was revealed about Ghazwa(غزوة) Hawazin(هوازن) or Hunain(حنين).

558
00:40:32,310 --> 00:40:33,842
It's called Hawazin(هوازن) and Hunain(حنين) .

559
00:40:34,103 --> 00:40:39,238
Hunain because it is the place, the location and Hawazin(هوازن) is the name of the tribe.

560
00:40:39,536 --> 00:40:40,567
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

561
00:40:40,748 --> 00:40:48,317
لَقَدْ نَصَرَكُمُ اللَّهُ فِي مَوَاطِنَ كَثِيرَةٍ ۙ وَيَوْمَ حُنَيْنٍ ۙ

562
00:40:48,626 --> 00:40:56,781
 وَيَوْمَ حُنَيْنٍ ۙ إِذْ أَعْجَبَتْكُمْ كَثْرَتُكُمْ فَلَمْ تُغْنِ عَنْكُمْ شَيْئًا

563
00:40:57,135 --> 00:41:05,490
وَضَاقَتْ عَلَيْكُمُ الْأَرْضُ بِمَا رَحُبَتْ ثُمَّ وَلَّيْتُمْ مُدْبِرِينَ

564
00:41:05,909 --> 00:41:14,132
ثُمَّ أَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ سَكِينَتَهُ عَلَىٰ رَسُولِهِ وَعَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ

565
00:41:14,511 --> 00:41:21,180
وَأَنْزَلَ جُنُودًا لَمْ تَرَوْهَا وَعَذَّبَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا ۚ

566
00:41:21,427 --> 00:41:26,913
 وَذَٰلِكَ جَزَاءُ الْكَافِرِينَ۝

567
00:41:27,429 --> 00:41:31,155
Assuredly, Allah did help you in many battlefields.

568
00:41:31,542 --> 00:41:36,838
And on the day of Hunain(حنين), behold your great numbers elated you

569
00:41:37,353 --> 00:41:43,329
but they availed you not the land for all that is wide did constrain you.

570
00:41:44,154 --> 00:41:46,289
And you turned back in retreat.

571
00:41:46,840 --> 00:41:50,637
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says: Behold you great numbers elated you.

572
00:41:51,688 --> 00:41:57,300
You felt confident, in the numbers that you have and that's where the problem is,

573
00:41:57,812 --> 00:42:00,929
if we feel that we will win, because of our numbers,

574
00:42:01,191 --> 00:42:03,973
if we feel that we will win because of our training,

575
00:42:04,071 --> 00:42:06,851
if we feel that we will win because of our technology,

576
00:42:07,183 --> 00:42:12,106
we feel that we will win because of our arms and weapons, we are mistaken.

577
00:42:12,669 --> 00:42:16,092
We win because of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

578
00:42:17,002 --> 00:42:24,827
And whenever, we attribute our victory to anything other than Allahعَزّوجَلّ, we will be defeated.

579
00:42:25,066 --> 00:42:26,871
The help of Allah will not be with us.

580
00:42:27,172 --> 00:42:29,082
Therefore, this is what counts.

581
00:42:29,440 --> 00:42:33,638
It is the Eeman(إيمان), it is the trust that we have in Allahعزوجل, the Tawaqul(توكل).

582
00:42:34,463 --> 00:42:36,352
It is our dependence on Him.

583
00:42:37,226 --> 00:42:39,801
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says that

584
00:42:39,825 --> 00:42:43,809
you thought that your numbers will give you victory, your numbers did you nothing.

585
00:42:44,693 --> 00:42:49,435
And then Allahعَزّوجَلّ says: Even the land became to constraint for you.

586
00:42:50,143 --> 00:42:51,688
You felt that you were so crowded,

587
00:42:51,712 --> 00:42:54,576
you felt that the land is not even enough for you, you had to flee.

588
00:42:55,653 --> 00:43:02,432
And then after that Allah says, but Allah did pour His calm on His Messenger and on the believers

589
00:43:02,721 --> 00:43:08,192
and sent down forces with which you saw not, He punish the unbelievers.

590
00:43:08,430 --> 00:43:11,946
Thus does, He reward those without faith.

591
00:43:12,647 --> 00:43:19,090
The people of Hawazin(هوازن) were defeated by a core group of the Muslim army,

592
00:43:19,114 --> 00:43:22,927
we said that the Muslim army was 12,000.

593
00:43:23,455 --> 00:43:27,098
However, the ones who were steadfast with Rasool Allah ﷺ

594
00:43:27,563 --> 00:43:34,022
after the big retreat that occurred, were between 80 to 100 Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

595
00:43:34,791 --> 00:43:41,331
And there was a core group among those, who were the firmest and never retreated.

596
00:43:41,355 --> 00:43:43,156
In fact, the only moved forward.

597
00:43:43,707 --> 00:43:48,327
And these are Rasool Allah ﷺ and his uncle and his cousin,

598
00:43:48,871 --> 00:43:54,797
and two or three other men next to them who were guarding Rasool Allah  صلوات الله وسلام عليه.

599
00:43:55,558 --> 00:44:00,375
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ called for Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار), specifically.

600
00:44:00,873 --> 00:44:04,497
And then he called for Al-Khazraj(الخزرج) and then a called for Bannu Najjar(بنونجار).

601
00:44:05,197 --> 00:44:08,556
These were the supporters of Rasool Allah ﷺ throughout the past years

602
00:44:08,580 --> 00:44:10,224
and they were his supporters now.

603
00:44:10,752 --> 00:44:13,311
And these are the ones, who defended Rasool Allah ﷺ

604
00:44:13,335 --> 00:44:19,025
and then defeated the huge army of the tribes of Hawazin(هوازن).

605
00:44:19,904 --> 00:44:23,946
So, Hawazin(هوازن) retreated, and we said that the leader was Malik Bin Auf An-Nasri(مالك بن عوف أنصري).

606
00:44:24,841 --> 00:44:32,080
So, what happened is Malik Bin Auf(مالك بن عوف) and the main body of the army retreated to At-Taef(ألطائف)

607
00:44:32,748 --> 00:44:35,633
and then they shut the doors of At-Taef(ألطائف).

608
00:44:35,695 --> 00:44:37,363
At-Taef(ألطائف) was a fortified city,

609
00:44:37,597 --> 00:44:43,494
while another branch of the army, a smaller branch, went to a place called Autaas(أوطاس).

610
00:44:43,741 --> 00:44:46,610
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ also split his army,

611
00:44:46,980 --> 00:44:54,268
the major part led by Rasool Allah ﷺ, followed Malik Bin Auf An-Nasri(مالك بن عوف أنصري) to At-Taef(الطائف),

612
00:44:54,382 --> 00:45:00,508
while a smaller group led by Abu Amir Al-Ashari(ابوعامرالاشعري), the uncle Abu Musa Al-Ashari(ابوموسى الاشعري), went to Autaas(أوطاس).

613
00:45:00,702 --> 00:45:07,176
We'll start first with this smaller Sariyyah(سريه), that went to Autaas(أوطاس), led by Abu Amir Al-Ashari رضي الله عنه.

614
00:45:07,631 --> 00:45:13,954
Among the disbelievers, who went to Autaas(أوطاس) was Duraid Bin Summah(دريد بن الصمة).

615
00:45:14,384 --> 00:45:18,292
Duraid Bin Summah(دريد بن الصمة) was with this small group of disbelievers that went to this area.

616
00:45:18,846 --> 00:45:22,686
Duraid Bin Summah(دريد بن الصمة) we mentioned him before, he was a very old man at that time.

617
00:45:23,101 --> 00:45:31,321
And he was a well known poet and also a very experienced and seasoned fighter.

618
00:45:32,028 --> 00:45:37,108
He as we mentioned before, had this discussion with Malik Bin Auf n-Nasri(مالك بن عوف أنصري),

619
00:45:37,995 --> 00:45:44,573
where he told him that it's a mistake to bring out the families and the wealth and to put them at such risk.

620
00:45:44,978 --> 00:45:45,778
And he told them that

621
00:45:45,802 --> 00:45:47,613
هَلْ يَرُدُّ الْمُنْهَزِمْ شَىءْ

622
00:45:47,653 --> 00:45:50,405
Does anything bring back the person who's on retreat.

623
00:45:51,034 --> 00:45:57,761
Anyway, Malik Bin Auf(مالك بن عوف) insisted, and it eventually turned out that the words of Duraid(دُرَيد) were true.

624
00:45:58,073 --> 00:46:02,003
Anyhow, let's see how the turn of events went from there.

625
00:46:02,491 --> 00:46:06,299
Duraid Bin Summah(دريد بن الصمة) was with this group that was in Autaas(أوطاس)

626
00:46:06,473 --> 00:46:11,989
one of the members of the Muslim army, his name is Rabia Bin Rafia As-Sulami(ربيعة بن رافيع ألسلمي),

627
00:46:12,173 --> 00:46:19,389
he found this camel with the compartment on top of it, which is used usually for women.

628
00:46:19,766 --> 00:46:23,524
So, he was leading this camel thinking that there is a woman in there,

629
00:46:23,974 --> 00:46:26,574
and he's taken her as a captive.

630
00:46:27,071 --> 00:46:31,227
When he had the woman or the camel, kneel down.

631
00:46:31,621 --> 00:46:35,337
And then he went to take a look inside the compartment to his amazement,

632
00:46:35,370 --> 00:46:37,747
he found that it wasn't a woman but it was an old man.

633
00:46:37,923 --> 00:46:40,453
So, he pulled the old man out of this compartment.

634
00:46:41,293 --> 00:46:45,011
So the old man asked him, What do you want to do, with me?

635
00:46:45,633 --> 00:46:46,969
He said: I want to kill you.

636
00:46:47,265 --> 00:46:48,153
He said: Who are you?

637
00:46:48,193 --> 00:46:52,289
 He said: I am Rabia Bin Rafia As-Sulami(ربيعة بن رافيع ألسلمي).

638
00:46:52,643 --> 00:46:56,432
And then he pulled out his sword and struck Duraid Bin Summah(دريد بن الصمة).

639
00:46:57,006 --> 00:47:00,686
The strike was not fatal, so Duraid Bin Summah(دريد بن الصمة) told him;

640
00:47:00,710 --> 00:47:02,315
بِئْسَ مَا صَلَحْتكَ اُمُّكْ

641
00:47:03,100 --> 00:47:05,658
Your mother did not arm you, right.

642
00:47:05,998 --> 00:47:09,862
And then he said: Here, take my sword from my saddle,

643
00:47:10,601 --> 00:47:14,533
strike me with it, hit over the spine, and below the skull.

644
00:47:14,928 --> 00:47:16,911
That's how I used to strike men.

645
00:47:17,587 --> 00:47:23,376
And then when you go back to your mother, tell her I killed Duraid Bin Summah(دريد بن الصمة).

646
00:47:24,013 --> 00:47:27,149
I swear many were the times, I defended your women.

647
00:47:27,392 --> 00:47:33,678
Duraid Bin Summah(دريد بن الصمة) was talking to a man, who is also a descendant of Hawazin(هوازن).

648
00:47:33,702 --> 00:47:37,867
These are clans, that are closely related, but this is a Muslim and Duraid(دُرَيْد) is a Kaafir(كافر).

649
00:47:38,184 --> 00:47:40,548
And Duraid(دُرَيْد) is telling him that there were days,

650
00:47:40,573 --> 00:47:44,599
when I fought for the sake of your people and for the sake of your women.

651
00:47:44,751 --> 00:47:46,065
Now, this is a young man.

652
00:47:46,662 --> 00:47:51,225
He doesn't know about this history, but Duraid(دُرَيْد) is telling him about it.

653
00:47:51,569 --> 00:47:56,242
Because he knows that the older people of his clan would know about it.

654
00:47:56,266 --> 00:48:00,491
So it's telling him when he go back to your mother tell her that I killed Duraid Bin Summah(دريد بن الصمة).

655
00:48:01,058 --> 00:48:05,994
So, he struck him as he was told, and Duraid(دُرَيْد) fell down dead.

656
00:48:06,326 --> 00:48:09,552
When he fell down, his private parts were exposed.

657
00:48:10,001 --> 00:48:16,386
So, this young man said: The skin which was high up between his thighs was like parchment,

658
00:48:16,853 --> 00:48:20,016
from having so often ridden on his horse bareback.

659
00:48:20,574 --> 00:48:27,523
The skin was so rough, because he used to ride on his horse without the saddle.

660
00:48:27,980 --> 00:48:33,195
We're talking about here a seasoned fighter, who has a long history behind him.

661
00:48:33,824 --> 00:48:37,010
Anyway, Ya'ani(يعني), we mentioned let's look at the turn of events

662
00:48:37,035 --> 00:48:39,261
Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله), the Aqdaar(أقدار) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

663
00:48:39,304 --> 00:48:47,078
Ya'ani(يعني) a man like Abu Talib(أبوطالب) just giving an example of how, we never know how the Qadar(قدر) of Allah turns out.

664
00:48:47,539 --> 00:48:51,813
And this means that a Muslim should always be prepared and ready

665
00:48:51,853 --> 00:48:56,245
and should always ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to give him Thabaat(ثبات), to give him steadfastness.

666
00:48:56,406 --> 00:49:01,515
Because you find that Abu Talib(ابو طالب), who for all of his life was supporting Rasool Allah ﷺ

667
00:49:02,145 --> 00:49:05,060
and preventing any harm from reaching to Him.

668
00:49:05,313 --> 00:49:07,819
He dies as a disbeliever,

669
00:49:08,162 --> 00:49:14,000
and then you have a person like Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان), who spent all of his life fighting against Muhammadﷺ,

670
00:49:14,248 --> 00:49:17,156
and then eventually at his old age, he becomes Muslim.

671
00:49:17,582 --> 00:49:25,784
So, here you have Malik Bin Auf(مالك بن عوف), who was the one, who caused this disaster, on the people of Hawazin(هوازن).

672
00:49:26,655 --> 00:49:30,753
And who insisted on following his wrong opinion.

673
00:49:31,100 --> 00:49:35,187
And on rejecting the opinion of Duraid Bin Summah(دريد بن الصمة), which was a wise opinion.

674
00:49:35,699 --> 00:49:40,303
Malik Bin Auf(مالك بن عوف), he ends up becoming a Muslim and we'll talk about how that happened.

675
00:49:40,537 --> 00:49:45,595
While Duraid Bin Summah(دريد بن الصمة), who was giving him the sound advice dies as a disbeliever.

676
00:49:46,316 --> 00:49:49,482
This young man Rabiya(ربيعة) went back to his mother

677
00:49:49,515 --> 00:49:52,482
and he told her, just like he was told by Duraid(دُرَيْد).

678
00:49:52,507 --> 00:49:54,499
He said: I have killed Duraid Bin Summah(دريد بن الصمة).

679
00:49:54,659 --> 00:49:58,906
She said: I swear he has freed, three of your mother's

680
00:49:59,339 --> 00:50:02,860
meaning three of your relatives, who are older than you.

681
00:50:02,884 --> 00:50:08,489
And this could refer to his mother or his grandmother's or his aunt's.

682
00:50:08,642 --> 00:50:12,307
Anyway, this is the story of Duraid Bin Summah(دريد بن الصمة).

683
00:50:12,484 --> 00:50:15,965
Abu Aamir(ابوعامر) who was the leader of the Sariyyah(سريه), he got shot in his knee.

684
00:50:16,148 --> 00:50:21,344
So Abu Musa Al-Ashari(ابوموسى الأشعري) his nephew came to him and said: O, my uncle, who shot you.

685
00:50:22,118 --> 00:50:25,743
So, Abu Aamir(ابوعامر) appointed to the man, who shot him.

686
00:50:26,254 --> 00:50:28,573
So, Abu Musa(ابوموسى) went running after him.

687
00:50:28,613 --> 00:50:30,589
And this narration is in Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(المسلم).

688
00:50:30,908 --> 00:50:32,169
Abu Musa(ابوموسى) followed the man.

689
00:50:32,631 --> 00:50:35,972
So, the man when he saw Abu Musa(ابوموسى) pursuing him, he fled.

690
00:50:36,330 --> 00:50:39,046
So, Abu Musa(ابوموسى) is running behind this man, and is telling him;

691
00:50:39,071 --> 00:50:41,830
اَلَا تَسْتَحِى؟ اَلَاتَثْبُتْ؟ اَلَسْتَ عَرَبِيًّا؟

692
00:50:42,425 --> 00:50:45,033
He told him, aren't you ashamed of yourself?

693
00:50:45,057 --> 00:50:48,289
Aren't you going to stand and fight? Aren't you an Arab man?

694
00:50:48,691 --> 00:50:52,955
So, when this man heard these challenging words from Abu Musa(ابوموسى),

695
00:50:53,193 --> 00:50:56,453
he turned around and came to fight Abu Musa(ابوموسى)

696
00:50:56,660 --> 00:50:59,200
they exchanged a few blows, and he was killed,

697
00:50:59,378 --> 00:51:01,074
Abu Musa(ابوموسى) killed this man.

698
00:51:01,183 --> 00:51:03,762
So, then Abu Musa(ابوموسى) went back to his uncle and told him,

699
00:51:03,947 --> 00:51:06,307
O uncle, I've killed the man, who killed you.

700
00:51:06,998 --> 00:51:11,645
And then Abu Aamir(ابوعامر) told Abu Musa(ابوموسى) to pull out the arrow from his knee.

701
00:51:11,844 --> 00:51:13,049
And when he did so,

702
00:51:13,553 --> 00:51:15,372
you know the arrow must be pulled out.

703
00:51:15,488 --> 00:51:18,715
But the thing is that the arrow has to pointed edges.

704
00:51:19,021 --> 00:51:23,699
 So, when you would go to pull it out, it could cause additional tearing.

705
00:51:23,985 --> 00:51:31,676
Anyway, when the arrow was pulled out, bleeding increased and Abu Aamir(ابوعامر) knew that he's dying.

706
00:51:31,908 --> 00:51:36,462
So, he told Abu Musa(ابوموسى), he told him give my Salams(سلام) to Rasool Allah ﷺ

707
00:51:36,982 --> 00:51:38,355
وَاسْئَلُه’ اَنْ يَسْتَغْفِرلِىْ

708
00:51:38,874 --> 00:51:41,969
And ask him to ask Allah to forgive me.

709
00:51:42,690 --> 00:51:45,114
And then after these words, he passed away.

710
00:51:45,519 --> 00:51:51,977
Abu Musa Al-Ashari رضي الله عنه, went to Rasool Ullah صلوات الله وسلام عليه, and told him the story

711
00:51:52,339 --> 00:51:54,850
and Rasool Allah ﷺ was sleeping on a bed

712
00:51:55,644 --> 00:52:01,237
that was made from ropes, these ropes were made from the leaves, dried leaves of date palms,

713
00:52:02,022 --> 00:52:05,463
and Rasool Allah ﷺ was sleeping on that bed and there is no mattress on it.

714
00:52:06,038 --> 00:52:11,080
And when he woke up, Abu Musa(ابوموسى) could see clearly the marks of the ropes

715
00:52:11,513 --> 00:52:15,055
on the side and the back of Rasool Ullah صلوات الله وسلام عليه.

716
00:52:15,700 --> 00:52:20,631
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ asked for some water and then Rasool Allah ﷺ made Wadhoo(وضؤ),

717
00:52:20,907 --> 00:52:25,466
and then he raised his hands, Abu Musa(ابوموسى) says until I could see his armpits

718
00:52:25,508 --> 00:52:29,848
meaning that Rasool Allah ﷺ was deeply involved in his Dua(دعا).

719
00:52:30,282 --> 00:52:34,764
And he said, O Allah, forgive this servant of Yours,

720
00:52:35,362 --> 00:52:41,235
اَللَّهُمَّ اَجْعَلْه’ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ فَوْقَ كَثِيْرٍ مِنْ خَلْقِكْ، اَوْ فَوْقَ كَثِيْرٍ مِنَّ النَّاسْ

721
00:52:41,619 --> 00:52:46,328
O Allah forgive the sins of your servant, Abu Aamir(ابوعامر),

722
00:52:46,770 --> 00:52:51,774
and make him above many of your creation, on the Day of Judgment.

723
00:52:52,005 --> 00:52:53,516
This was a great Dua(دعا),

724
00:52:53,848 --> 00:53:00,546
that was made by Rasool Allah ﷺ, for the Mujahid(مجاهد) and the Shaheed(شهيد), Abu Aamir Al-Ashari رضي الله عنه

725
00:53:01,268 --> 00:53:04,821
to make him on top of many of the creation of the Day of Judgment,

726
00:53:04,893 --> 00:53:08,749
what a great honor to be in that high status on the Day Of Judgment,

727
00:53:08,789 --> 00:53:12,221
and that's all what counts, your position on the Day of Judgment,

728
00:53:12,738 --> 00:53:21,140
people are fighting for position in Duniya(دنيا), forgetting that the most important is what will happen on the Day of Judgment.

729
00:53:21,601 --> 00:53:25,376
And that's why they say that the Bedouin who made the Dua(دعا) of;

730
00:53:25,491 --> 00:53:32,365
O Allah, make the best of my life, the end of it, and make the best of my deeds, the last of them

731
00:53:32,639 --> 00:53:35,331
and make the best of my days, the day I will meet you.

732
00:53:35,452 --> 00:53:37,499
They said this is a very wise Dua(دعا),

733
00:53:37,597 --> 00:53:41,378
because the most important day of all days is the day of judgment,

734
00:53:41,616 --> 00:53:46,938
because it's equivalent to all of our days combined, the day of judgment is 50,000 years long.

735
00:53:47,410 --> 00:53:52,397
So, when Allahعَزّوجَلّ will make that day, the best day, that is what you want.

736
00:53:53,334 --> 00:54:00,290
So, when Abu Musa(ابوموسى) saw Rasool Allah ﷺ making this lovely Dua(دعا) for his uncle, Abu Aamir(ابوعامر).

737
00:54:00,315 --> 00:54:05,427
Abu Musa Al-Ashari(ابوموسى الأشعري), he wanted to take advantage of this great opportunity that opened up for him.

738
00:54:05,740 --> 00:54:07,821
So, he said: O Rasool Allah ﷺ make Dua(دعا) for me.

739
00:54:08,334 --> 00:54:09,691
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

740
00:54:10,140 --> 00:54:12,985
اَللَّهُمَ اغْفِرْ لِعَبْدِالله بن قَيْس

741
00:54:13,018 --> 00:54:14,755
O Allah forgive Abdullah Bin Qais(عبد الله بن قيس).

742
00:54:14,779 --> 00:54:17,519
Abdullah Bin Qais(عبد الله بن قيس) is the name of Abu Musa(ابوموسى), Abu Musa(ابوموسى) is his Kunniyah(كنيه).

743
00:54:17,672 --> 00:54:20,292
O Allah forgive the sins of Abdullah Bin Qais(عبد الله بن قيس).

744
00:54:20,316 --> 00:54:23,355
وَاَدْخِلْه’ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ مُدْخَلًا كَرِيْمًا

745
00:54:23,514 --> 00:54:28,300
And O Allah give him a noble admittance, on the day of Judgment

746
00:54:28,324 --> 00:54:33,717
or enter him a good entrance on the Day of Judgment, meaning to enter into paradise.

747
00:54:33,846 --> 00:54:36,058
So, the narrator of this Hadith(حديث), Abu Burda(ابوبردة) says;

748
00:54:36,082 --> 00:54:39,895
One Dua(دعا) was made for Abu Aamir(ابوعامر) and the other Dua(دعا) was made for Abu Musa(ابوموسى).

749
00:54:40,300 --> 00:54:42,690
This is the story of Autaas(أوطاس).

750
00:54:42,714 --> 00:54:46,610
Now, we move on to the main branch of both armies,

751
00:54:46,634 --> 00:54:50,197
which would lead us to Ghazwa At-Taef(غزوة ألطائف), the Battle of At-Taef(الطائف),

752
00:54:50,654 --> 00:54:51,865
the books of Seerah(سيرة) says;

753
00:54:51,889 --> 00:54:53,575
حَاصَرَهَا حِصَارً شَدِيْدَا

754
00:54:53,599 --> 00:54:58,939
Rasool Allah ﷺ put a very strict, siege on At-Taef(ألطائف) .

755
00:54:59,116 --> 00:55:00,687
In fact, Ibn Hishaam(إبن هشام) says;

756
00:55:00,800 --> 00:55:07,441
فَحَدَثَنِيْ مِنْ اَثِقْ بِهِ النَّبِيْ صلى الله عليه وسلم اَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ مَا فِيْ الْاِسْلَامِ بِلْ مَنْجَنِيْقْ

757
00:55:08,078 --> 00:55:13,333
Ibn Hishaam(إبن هشام), the scholar and writer of Seerah(سيرة), the student of Ibn Is'haaq(إبن إسحاق), he says

758
00:55:13,358 --> 00:55:15,597
I was told by whom, I trust

759
00:55:16,211 --> 00:55:23,408
that the first one in Islam to use and throw the catapult is Rasool Allah ﷺ.

760
00:55:23,433 --> 00:55:28,193
Rasool Allah ﷺ is the first one in Islam to use the catapult.

761
00:55:28,815 --> 00:55:36,577
This was a siege equipment that was used to hurl stones at the walls of At-Taef(ألطائف)

762
00:55:36,601 --> 00:55:39,580
and the first one to use it, was Rasool Allah ﷺ.

763
00:55:39,771 --> 00:55:44,079
And I say in Islam, meaning that it was used before, it's not like they invented it.

764
00:55:44,103 --> 00:55:47,796
But the first one to use it among the Muslims was Rasool Allah ﷺ.

765
00:55:48,746 --> 00:55:52,285
And this was the first Ghazwa(غزوة) in which it was used.

766
00:55:52,437 --> 00:55:56,774
Now, the catapult, when it fires,

767
00:55:57,442 --> 00:56:02,867
it would hurl this stones, either at the wall or inside the fortress.

768
00:56:03,406 --> 00:56:06,609
And you did not really see when it hits inside the fort.

769
00:56:06,895 --> 00:56:10,035
mean we're talking about a whole city inside these walls.

770
00:56:10,773 --> 00:56:17,159
When this missile arrives in the city, it can hit anywhere it could hit home,

771
00:56:17,663 --> 00:56:22,122
it could hit the street, it could hit the market, it could strike anywhere.

772
00:56:22,697 --> 00:56:26,814
And it could cause collateral damage that is not originally intended.

773
00:56:26,838 --> 00:56:29,379
For example, it could strike women and children,

774
00:56:29,680 --> 00:56:33,553
even though the intention of the one, who was striking is not to hit them.

775
00:56:33,698 --> 00:56:38,222
But it's something that would land out of your line of sight.

776
00:56:38,246 --> 00:56:40,140
So, you don't really know where it falls.

777
00:56:40,238 --> 00:56:49,259
And therefore this was used as evidence by contemporary scholars of the legality of using modern weaponry

778
00:56:49,714 --> 00:56:54,816
 that is similar to the catapult in its method of striking,

779
00:56:55,102 --> 00:56:58,828
which is different than using an arrow where you see your target and you fire at.

780
00:56:59,215 --> 00:57:07,099
This is something that is similar to some modern firepower that ends up hitting the enemy indiscriminately.

781
00:57:07,729 --> 00:57:13,972
So again, this is one of many other evidence that is used by modern scholars in this regard.

782
00:57:14,448 --> 00:57:21,598
Now, even though the catapult was being used, and it was fired, and it was ramming At-Taef(ألطائف)

783
00:57:21,622 --> 00:57:25,881
they didn't give up and they had archers on the walls.

784
00:57:25,906 --> 00:57:29,426
And in one narration, it says that the Muslims were within range,

785
00:57:29,664 --> 00:57:31,671
and they were being struck by these arrows.

786
00:57:31,736 --> 00:57:38,243
So, they had to retreat and move out of range and then, the Sahabah(صحابه) use what is called the Dababah(دبابه),

787
00:57:38,481 --> 00:57:42,348
and this was a wooden structure where some Sahabah(صحابه) would enter into

788
00:57:42,984 --> 00:57:47,082
and then they would use as a cover to protect them from arrows

789
00:57:47,106 --> 00:57:50,586
until they can reach to the wall and be close to it.

790
00:57:50,910 --> 00:57:55,757
But the thing is that the people At-Taef(ألطائف) used a weapon against Ad-Dababah(ألدبابه),

791
00:57:55,977 --> 00:58:01,972
they were using thorny pieces of iron that were heated in fire.

792
00:58:02,382 --> 00:58:06,221
So, these pieces of iron would strike against Ad-Dababah(ألدبابه) and burn it

793
00:58:06,639 --> 00:58:11,481
and then would penetrated it and reach to the ones, who are inside.

794
00:58:11,900 --> 00:58:15,098
So, it injured some of the Sahabah(صحابه), so they had to retreat

795
00:58:15,123 --> 00:58:17,580
this weapon was proving ineffective.

796
00:58:17,612 --> 00:58:22,403
When this happened, Rasool Allah ﷺ ordered that

797
00:58:22,428 --> 00:58:27,268
the grape vines of At-Taef(ألطائف) which were outside of the city to be cut down

798
00:58:27,483 --> 00:58:29,597
and they cut down some of them.

799
00:58:30,217 --> 00:58:36,537
Again, this is similar to what Rasool Allah ﷺ did in the siege of the Jews of Bannu Nadhir(بنو نضير)

800
00:58:36,602 --> 00:58:40,777
when he ordered that the palm trees be cut down, as a weapon against the enemy,

801
00:58:40,817 --> 00:58:45,974
 because when they see that their livelihood is being burned down,

802
00:58:46,182 --> 00:58:50,520
it weakens their morale and willingness to carry on with the siege.

803
00:58:51,056 --> 00:58:54,113
We'll read this narration from Musnad Imam Ahmad(مسند إمام أحمد).

804
00:58:54,626 --> 00:58:56,559
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

805
00:58:56,849 --> 00:59:00,098
مَنْ بَلَغَ بِسَهْمٍ فَلَه’ دَرَجَةِ فِيْ الْجَنَّةْ

806
00:59:00,829 --> 00:59:05,520
The one, who shoots an arrow and the arrow reaches its target,

807
00:59:05,981 --> 00:59:09,680
will get one level in paradise, with each arrow you get one level.

808
00:59:10,224 --> 00:59:12,321
That is how great the Ajr(أجر) is.?

809
00:59:12,839 --> 00:59:21,337
And one can make Qiyass(قياس) of this on modern forms of weaponry that could be shot similar to the way an arrow is shot.

810
00:59:21,816 --> 00:59:26,244
Now, the narrator of the Hadith(حديث), Abu Najieh Al-Salami(أبو نجيح ألسلمي), said;

811
00:59:26,269 --> 00:59:34,440
I have shot 16 arrows and all of them reach the targets, so that is 16 levels in Jannah(جنة).

812
00:59:34,959 --> 00:59:37,698
Just like that! That's just how great the Ajr(أجر) is.

813
00:59:38,082 --> 00:59:39,653
Then Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

814
00:59:40,155 --> 00:59:43,261
وَمَنْ شَابَ شَيْبَةً فِيْ سَبِيْلِ الله

815
00:59:43,330 --> 00:59:45,158
كَانَتْ لَه’ نُوْرًا يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةْ

816
00:59:45,920 --> 00:59:52,457
And whoever grows one gray hair, white hair Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(في سبيل الله) and

817
00:59:52,576 --> 00:59:56,764
Ibn Hajar Al-Asqalani(إبن حجرألعسقلاني) says; Whenever Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) is mentioned,

818
00:59:57,057 --> 00:59:59,534
it is referring to fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

819
00:59:59,867 --> 01:00:04,429
Rasool Allah ﷺ says whoever grows one grey hair in Islam,

820
01:00:04,771 --> 01:00:07,153
it will be light for him on the Day of Judgment.

821
01:00:07,389 --> 01:00:10,792
و أيُّما رجُلٍ مُسلِمٍ أعتقَ رجُلًا مسلِمًا

822
01:00:11,206 --> 01:00:17,630
فإنَّ اللَّهَ عز و جل جاعِلٌ وفاءَ كلِّ عظمٍ مِن عظامِهِ عَظمًا من عظامِ محرَّر

823
01:00:18,222 --> 01:00:22,059
منَ النَّارِ ، وأيُّما امرأةٍ مُسْلِمَة أعتقتِ امرأةً مُسْلِمَةً

824
01:00:22,317 --> 01:00:29,536
فإنَّ اللَّهَ عز و جل جاعلٌ وفاءَ كلِّ عظمٍ من عظامِها عظمًا من عظامِ محرَّرھا منَ النَّارِ

825
01:00:29,736 --> 01:00:33,002
Rasool Allah ﷺ says; And any Muslim, who frees a slave,

826
01:00:33,304 --> 01:00:39,910
then every bone of that slave will free the equivalent bone in him on the Day of Judgment, from hellfire.

827
01:00:40,119 --> 01:00:46,762
And the same thing Rasool Allah ﷺ mentions about a woman, who frees a Muslim woman.

828
01:00:47,108 --> 01:00:50,193
So, this also shows the great Ajr(أجر) of freeing slaves

829
01:00:50,218 --> 01:00:53,794
and this is what encouraged the Muslims to free slaves throughout the history

830
01:00:53,984 --> 01:00:56,963
and probably there is no nation in history that has freed,

831
01:00:57,362 --> 01:01:03,862
so many slaves for, no economical reason, for no worldly reason but to please Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

832
01:01:04,146 --> 01:01:07,458
You find that only with the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ.

833
01:01:07,954 --> 01:01:09,064
Al-Waqide'e(ألوقعدي) says;

834
01:01:09,245 --> 01:01:14,870
لَمَّا مَضَتْ خَمْسَ عَشْرَةَ لَيْلَةَ مِنْ حِصَارِ الطَّائفْ اِسْتَشَارَ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم نوفل ابن معاويه الديلي

835
01:01:15,286 --> 01:01:20,904
فقال: "يَا نوفل مَا تَرَى فِى الْمُقَامِ عَلَيْهِمْ"؟ ،قال : يا رسول الله ثَعَلَبٌ فِيْ جُحَرْ

836
01:01:21,235 --> 01:01:23,688
اِنْ اَقَمْتَ عَلَيْهِ اَخَذْتَه’ وَاِنْ تَرَكْتَه’ لَمْ يَضُرُّكْ

837
01:01:24,326 --> 01:01:27,715
The siege carried on for 15 days and they were getting nowhere

838
01:01:28,059 --> 01:01:32,374
and the people of Taef(طائف) were still firm and strong in their resistance of the siege.

839
01:01:32,685 --> 01:01:37,097
At-Taef(ألطائف) was a fortified city surrounded by wall, so they were well protected.

840
01:01:37,410 --> 01:01:46,875
And after 15 days, Rasool Allah ﷺ sought the Shura(شورى), the advice of Muawiyyah Bin Nofal Ad-Dahli(نوفل بن معاويه ألدئلي),

841
01:01:47,135 --> 01:01:51,605
he told them, what do you think about staying and continuing to the siege?

842
01:01:51,940 --> 01:01:57,079
So, Nofal(نوفل) said: O Messenger of Allah, they are a fox in a hole,

843
01:01:57,569 --> 01:01:59,495
they are just like a fox in a hole.

844
01:01:59,770 --> 01:02:04,317
If you stay at it, you will take it and if you leave it, it won't harm you anymore.

845
01:02:04,892 --> 01:02:09,413
What Nofal(نوفل) is saying, is that eventually it will fall but you'll have to carry on the siege.

846
01:02:09,641 --> 01:02:12,950
But if you leave it, it won't harm you, because they're just like a fox in a hole.

847
01:02:13,650 --> 01:02:17,689
They had been weakened so much and all of the people surrounding us, have become Muslim,

848
01:02:17,778 --> 01:02:21,614
that even if you left them alone, they wouldn't have any ability to harm the Muslims.

849
01:02:21,769 --> 01:02:24,150
In Al-Bukhari(البخاريْ), Ibn Umar(ابن عمر) narrates that

850
01:02:24,239 --> 01:02:28,997
لَمَّا كَانَ رسول الله صلي الله عليه وسلم بالِطَّائِف، اِنَّا قَافِلُوْنَ غَدّاً ، اِنْ شَاءَ الله

851
01:02:29,237 --> 01:02:32,311
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Tomorrow In Sha Allah(إن شاءالله) we will leave.

852
01:02:32,809 --> 01:02:33,804
فَثَقُلَ عَلَيْهِمْ

853
01:02:33,897 --> 01:02:37,300
This was a very heavy news on the Sahabah(صحابه), it was like a burden on them.

854
01:02:37,866 --> 01:02:42,207
And they said; Ya Rasool Allah, we leave without opening.

855
01:02:42,609 --> 01:02:44,550
لَا نَبْرَحُ اَوْ نَفْتَحَهْا؟

856
01:02:44,756 --> 01:02:47,144
We should not leave until, we open the city.

857
01:02:47,819 --> 01:02:51,467
Meaning, they just came out of victory after victory, they had the victory of Fateh(فتح) Makkah,

858
01:02:51,830 --> 01:02:53,463
and they have the victory of Hawazin(هوازن).

859
01:02:53,673 --> 01:02:57,350
And now, they wanted to get this third victory of opening At-Taef(ألطائف)

860
01:02:57,696 --> 01:03:01,280
and they still have the patience and the willingness to carry on.

861
01:03:01,485 --> 01:03:05,085
So, they didn't like the offer of leaving.

862
01:03:05,380 --> 01:03:06,934
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

863
01:03:06,981 --> 01:03:08,167
فاَغْدُوْا عَلَى الْقِتَالْ

864
01:03:08,192 --> 01:03:10,295
Then tomorrow go and fight.

865
01:03:11,001 --> 01:03:15,002
And Ghadoo(غدُّو) is leaving in the early hours of the day to go and fight.

866
01:03:15,106 --> 01:03:17,101
These were the instructions of Rasool Allah ﷺ

867
01:03:17,234 --> 01:03:22,787
قَالَ: فَغَدَوْ فَقَاتلُوْهُمْ قِتَالًا شَدِيْدًا فَكَثُرَفِيْهِمْ اَلْجِرَاحَاتْ

868
01:03:23,157 --> 01:03:27,441
So, next day they went and they fought and it was a very strong fight

869
01:03:27,648 --> 01:03:32,149
and many of them became injured, on this day, Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

870
01:03:32,465 --> 01:03:34,740
اِنَّا قَافِلُوْنَ غَدّاً ، اِنْ شَاءَ الله

871
01:03:35,021 --> 01:03:37,945
We will leave tomorrow by the will of Allah.

872
01:03:38,036 --> 01:03:39,109
قَالَ: فَسَكَتوا

873
01:03:39,134 --> 01:03:42,101
Ibn Umar(ابن عمر) said: They were silent and quiet,

874
01:03:42,234 --> 01:03:43,427
فَضَحِكَ رَسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم

875
01:03:43,452 --> 01:03:44,742
Rasool Allah ﷺ laughed,

876
01:03:45,137 --> 01:03:48,797
he laughed because yesterday, they said: We don't want to leave

877
01:03:49,053 --> 01:03:56,870
and today because they were injured and in that stiff fighting, they liked the offer of retreating.

878
01:03:57,942 --> 01:04:01,578
When Rasool Allah ﷺ was laying siege to At-Taef(ألطائف)

879
01:04:01,929 --> 01:04:06,793
an announcement was made that whoever surrenders, they will be freed.

880
01:04:07,402 --> 01:04:08,615
Even if they're slaves.

881
01:04:09,206 --> 01:04:14,055
So, one of the ones who came down was Abu Bakra رضي الله عنه,

882
01:04:14,309 --> 01:04:19,352
who became one of the scholars and narrators of the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

883
01:04:19,614 --> 01:04:23,678
Abu Bakra(أبوبكرة), Bakra(بكرة) is when you have a rope coming down,

884
01:04:24,160 --> 01:04:28,642
and it's rolling on that piece of iron, that is called a Bakra(بكرة).

885
01:04:28,930 --> 01:04:35,192
And he was given that title on the day of At-Taef(ألطائف) because he came down from the wall using a rope,

886
01:04:35,232 --> 01:04:38,560
 so he was given that nickname of Abu Bakra(أبوبكرة)

887
01:04:39,419 --> 01:04:44,100
and Rasool Allah ﷺ freed him, so he was freed after this incident.

888
01:04:44,249 --> 01:04:47,423
And there were some others also who surrendered on that day.

889
01:04:48,146 --> 01:04:51,078
Abu Bakra(أبوبكرة) says that he heard Rasool Allah ﷺ say then;

890
01:04:51,549 --> 01:04:55,200
مَنِّ دَعَى اِلَى غَيْرِ اَبِيْهِ وَهُوَ يَعْلَمُه’ فِلْجَنَّةْ عَلَيْهَا حَرَامْ

891
01:04:55,512 --> 01:05:03,247
Anyone who claims to be the father of someone other than his real father, while knowing the truth will be denied paradise.

892
01:05:03,686 --> 01:05:08,439
So, this is a warning against anybody claiming that someone else is his father,

893
01:05:08,844 --> 01:05:12,597
other than his original father, it's a sin to do so.

894
01:05:12,758 --> 01:05:16,908
Rasool Allah ﷺ says that such a person will be denied paradise.

895
01:05:17,984 --> 01:05:25,131
At-Taef(ألطائف), dear brothers and sisters, was the last Ghazwa(غزوة), that Rasool Allah ﷺ fought with the Arabs,

896
01:05:25,344 --> 01:05:29,747
this was the end of the wars with the Arabs.

897
01:05:30,077 --> 01:05:33,859
After that there were small skirmishes but there were no more Ghazawaat(غزوات).

898
01:05:34,460 --> 01:05:38,321
Now, a new front will open, a new frontier

899
01:05:38,971 --> 01:05:46,412
and that is the frontier with the Roman Empire and that is the Ghazwaa(غزوة) Of Tabook(تبوك).

900
01:05:46,886 --> 01:05:51,674
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

901
01:05:52,071 --> 01:05:54,054
اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمةُ الله وَبَرَكَاتُه

